''   Started.... 04 Oct 2026
''   Updated.... 04 Oct 2026 -- task 3679 phase 1 (SRC_REV 1, fmt 1): the skeleton, the per-motor block and the
''               hall-map leg (L-hallmap) with its two cells, R23-SGL-ENCCHK and R23-SGL-SECTOR
''               04 Oct 2026 -- task 3679 phase 2a (SRC_REV 2, fmt 2): the hall map reads the PASM-latched edges
''               (isp_bench_encoder takeEdge()); the hands-off measuring legs L-mininc, L-ladder (L2, the feedforward
''               line, the reserve ceiling, the misdial check), L-ramp (L7, the reversal) and L-stops (L8); cells
''               R23-SGL-MININC, -FOLLOW, -MISDIAL, -SMOOTH, -RAMPARR, -STOPROT, -STOPTIME
''               04 Oct 2026 -- task 3679 phase 2b (SRC_REV 3, fmt 3): L-coast (L1, the coast-down after the guarded
''               testForceFault()), L-offscan (L3, the offset scan, the lead check and the hall zero at speed), L-passprb
''               (plan sec 1.4, the drive pass's period on the encoder), the front cog's statistics after every leg;
''               cells R23-SGL-COAST, -LEADMOVE, -PASSPRD; the misdial check's records carry the inputs to refit Ke
''               04 Oct 2026 -- task 3679 phase 2c (SRC_REV 4, fmt 4): the attended legs, each its own tier, on the
''               operator panel sgpanel (tools/gen_single_assets.py): L-handload (L5, the hand load at low speed),
''               L-heldpush (L6, the held stop pushed by hand), and the OPTIONAL L-sag (L4) and L-pinch (L2b); a measure
''               cog drives and samples while cog 0 runs the panel; cells R23-SGL-LIMHOLD, -BLKSTOP, -HOLDRISE,
''               -HOLDSLIP, -SAGTYPE. The lead check and the Z reference judge the DUTY fit's vertex (arbiter decision
''               D9, LEADMOVE_FITQ), the DC-link fit's recorded beside it
''               04 Oct 2026 -- task 3686 (SRC_REV 5, fmt 5): the D2 QUALIFICATION (plan sec 7): L-wiring (the public
''               start path and checkWiring()) and L-power (driveAtPower() rungs judged on the encoder), cells
''               R23-SGL-START, -POWER, -TOPSPD; -D SINGLE_QUALIFY builds the misdial check on the fitted Ke
''               (KE_FITTED_MV_PER_KRPM, arbiter decision D5); the exclusion check corrected six cells whose negative
''               read NOMEAS: RAMPARR, STOPROT / STOPTIME, LIMHOLD, HOLDRISE, HOLDSLIP
''               04 Oct 2026 -- task 3685 review (SRC_REV 6): ofsFit()'s constant term used the wrong minor (S1 x T2 for
''               T1 x S2), so B1-OFSFIT's rms, vertex standard error and resolved flag were wrong whenever the points were
''               not symmetric about the shipped offset; the vertex was right. D1 (SRC_REV 4) records every point
''               (B1-OFSPT), so its fits are re-done at the evaluation
''
'' =================================================================================================

{ WHY THIS RUN

  DOCs/plans/DOCO-AND-CLOCK-SPRINT-PLAN.md sec 4. The motor-adoption tool (sec 8) is generalised from two measured motors.
  The 6.5in instruments hard-code the 6.5in's numbers and two wheels; this harness measures the DocoEng 4k-rpm motor on the
  Doco bench (one motor, P16 board, a Rev A, a TOLD drive voltage, the 360 P/R shaft encoder on P48/P49) and keeps EVERY
  number that belongs to the motor in ONE block, "the Doco's numbers" below. Everything there that differs from the 6.5in
  instruments is listed, as it is changed, in the plan's sec 4 "Edited from the 6.5in instruments": that list is the
  motor-adoption tool's specification.

  LEGS. Each leg is a labelled record set and, where a judgement is possible, a cell. A leg is compiled in by its own
  -D SINGLE_PART_* symbol, and main() runs, in a fixed order, every leg the image carries -- so one tier may chain every
  leg that needs nothing from the operator (doctrine overlay P1: a command boundary goes where he must act, and nowhere
  else), and a leg may also be built alone. The legs, in the order main() runs them:
    SINGLE_PART_WIRING    L-wiring (task 3686, plan sec 7), run at the start, before the rest zero is read: the public
                          start path's verdict (start() with its checks refusing, getHealth()) and checkWiring()'s
                          walk, its HLT_WIRING verdict, with the encoder's travel beside it (R23-SGL-START)
    SINGLE_PART_HALLMAP   L-hallmap: the encoder angle at every hall edge, both directions, two crawl speeds; the
                          encoder self-check; each of the 24 sectors' width against 15 degrees; the hall pattern's zero
                          per direction in the encoder's frame (phase 1)
    SINGLE_PART_MININC    L-mininc (PL-71): a descending sweep of crawl rates each sign, from rest, until one does not
                          turn steadily on the encoder; the smallest steady one is the minimum (R23-SGL-MININC)
    SINGLE_PART_POWER     L-power (task 3686, plan sec 7): driveAtPower() at DAT powerPcts (25, 50, 75 and the row's
                          top power) each power sign, each from rest, held >= 5 s; the encoder's speed against the
                          increment the library wrote for the power (R23-SGL-POWER)
    SINGLE_PART_LADDER    L-ladder (the analysis's L2): rungs at 25/50/75/100 % of the row's shipped ceiling (and, from
                          12 V up, extension rungs to 400e6, never past PK1_CAP_INCR), each entered from rest on the
                          built-in ramp AND by a step from the rung below, held >= 5 s; the feedforward line, the
                          reserve ceiling, the misdial check (R23-SGL-FOLLOW, -MISDIAL, -SMOOTH, -TOPSPD)
    SINGLE_PART_RAMP      L-ramp (L7): power to the row's top from rest on the built-in ramp, then stopMotor(); and a
                          reversal at the top (R23-SGL-RAMPARR, -SMOOTH, -TOPSPD)
    SINGLE_PART_STOPS     L-stops (L8): stopAfterRotation(N) and stopAfterTime(T) armed at rest, at the top and at a
                          crawl, each sign; the encoder's rest against the limit (R23-SGL-STOPROT, -STOPTIME)
    SINGLE_PART_COAST     L-coast (L1, at the 12 V and 24 V rows only): steady at 25, 50 and 100 % of the row, each
                          sign, the fault response set to FR_SHIPPED with the bridge floated, then the guarded
                          testForceFault(): the encoder at 2 kHz until the shaft rests -- Tc/J and Bv/J are fitted from
                          it offline (R23-SGL-COAST judges the 100 % coast against the model's bracket)
    SINGLE_PART_OFFSCAN   L-offscan (L3, at the 12 V and 24 V rows only): at 25, 50 and 100 %, each sign, the offset
                          stepped 5 degrees at a time over +-30 of the shipped one; the DC link, duty and the hall zero
                          at speed per point; the current minimum per speed (the magnet reference for Z), and whether
                          it moves with speed (R23-SGL-LEADMOVE, the lead check). The shipped offsets are restored on
                          every exit
    SINGLE_PART_PASSPROBE L-passprb (plan sec 1.4): a constant command each sign for 10 s, the encoder's speed against
                          the increment x the pass rate of the ACTUAL frame (R23-SGL-PASSPRD); one tier per clock name
    SINGLE_PART_HANDLOAD  L-handload (L5, at the 12 V and 24 V rows only), ATTENDED: power 10 (~200-240 rpm), the
                          operator slows the shaft by hand to a stall; under testSetCurrentLimits(4, 4), then (2, 2),
                          then at 12 V only and only when the leg's charge cap allows, the default limits, briefly. The
                          blocked stop's latch against the last hall tick, the DC link, duty, fold and limit-hold
                          counts, the shaft's creep on the encoder (R23-SGL-LIMHOLD, -BLKSTOP)
    SINGLE_PART_HELDPUSH  L-heldpush (L6, at the 12 V and 24 V rows only), ATTENDED: holdAtStop(TRUE) at rest at the hold
                          defaults; the operator turns the shaft slowly by hand, one way, then the other, until the hold
                          gives way; the encoder angle at every hall edge, testGetHold(), getHoldStatus()
                          (R23-SGL-HOLDRISE, -HOLDSLIP)
    SINGLE_PART_SAG       L-sag (L4, OPTIONAL: arbiter decision D4, the act is confirmed with Stephen on the run sheet
                          first; at the 22.2 V and 18.5 V rows only), ATTENDED: at the row's top the operator turns the
                          bench supply down ~1 V/s until the speed is lost; fault first or slip first (R23-SGL-SAGTYPE)
    SINGLE_PART_PINCH     L-pinch (L2b, OPTIONAL as L-sag; at the 18.5 V row only), ATTENDED: at the row's top a cloth
                          pinch on the bare shaft end for 1-2 s; the DC link and duty loaded against unloaded (records)
  After every leg, at rest, B1-FRONT prints the front cog's statistics (testGetFrontStats()): the worst pass is the clock
  floor's input (plan sec 13). The hands-off legs need nothing from the operator; tools/bench-run.sh chains them all in
  one tier per voltage (single-measure-<voltage>). The four ATTENDED legs are each their own tier and never in
  single-measure (doctrine overlay P1: a command boundary goes where the operator must act).
  THE D2 QUALIFICATION (task 3686, plan sec 7): single-qualify-<voltage> chains the hands-off qualification legs --
  L-wiring, L-power, L-ladder, L-ramp, L-stops -- under -D SINGLE_QUALIFY, which builds the misdial check on the
  fitted Ke (KE_IS_FITTED TRUE, +-30 per mille); the hand-load criteria at 12 V and 24 V are single-handload and
  single-heldpush, reused, not duplicated. Each sec 7 criterion and the cell that judges it:
    the start checks and checkWiring() pass ......... R23-SGL-START (new)
    each power rung holds speed, encoder, 3 % ....... R23-SGL-POWER (new); R23-SGL-FOLLOW judges by increment
    ramps arrive within 10 % of the prediction ...... R23-SGL-RAMPARR
    stopAfterTime / stopAfterRotation at rest ....... R23-SGL-STOPTIME, R23-SGL-STOPROT
    the ceiling: no lag fault, no re-sync ........... R23-SGL-SMOOTH (NEG, POS, REVERSAL)
    the ceiling: rate on the speed law .............. R23-SGL-TOPSPD (new; NEG, POS, REVERSAL)
    the misdial check passes ........................ R23-SGL-MISDIAL, fitted
    12 V / 24 V hand load: the limit holds .......... R23-SGL-LIMHOLD (single-handload)
    the blocked shaft latches in 988-1,168 ms ....... R23-SGL-BLKSTOP (single-handload)
    the hold resists a push within its defaults ..... R23-SGL-HOLDRISE, R23-SGL-HOLDSLIP (single-heldpush)
  THE ATTENDED LEGS' PANEL (doctrine overlay P7, DOCs/procedures/PLOT-DISPLAY-RULES.md): one PLOT window, sgpanel, built
  on the supplied crop-and-overlay technique (DOCs/REF-NO-COMMIT/dbg-display-theory/) as T0-24's proven t0stop panel is
  (test_bench_t0.spin2), from the generated tables of tools/gen_single_assets.py. Every operator action is a titled
  button hit-tested through PC_MOUSE under cartesian 1; NO KEY is read. Each step is INTRO (START STEP) -> SETUP ->
  ACT -> (the sag's RESTORE) -> RESULT (REDO STEP / NEXT STEP, FINISH on the last): he ends every step he takes part
  in, or a sensor sees him finish -- the blocked stop's latch, the hold giving way and the encoder still, the speed
  lost -- and the result stays until he chooses. Only live buttons are drawn; every click is logged (B1-UI) and every
  screen (B1-SCREEN), after the screen, at rest. THE COGS (T0-24's split, PL-127): cog 0 runs the panel and prints
  every record; the measure cog (sgWorker()) drives, samples and guards every SAMPLE_MS and PRINTS NOTHING, so no
  debug() can wait on the panel's mouse read (P2-HAZARD-REGISTER DBG-10) while the motor turns.
  THE COLD BACK-EMF Z IS NOT BUILT (plan sec 4, sec 13): the arithmetic is at CON { the Doco's numbers }, COLD Z.
  THE REFERENCE LEGS RECORD TODAY'S BEHAVIOUR on the shipped tables (D1's "before"): a FAIL there is a finding about the
  drive, not a defect of this harness.

  SAFETY, because the operator is not at the controls: the board is READ before anything is started and must be the
  bench's EXPECTED_BOARD; the motor runs under a TEST current limit (testSetCurrentLimits(), TEST_PEAK_A / TEST_CONT_A)
  from the first leg; an absolute current abort and a run charge cap, both in milliamps and converted to the sense
  millivolts THROUGH THE DETECTED BOARD (Rev A 5 mV/A, Rev B 150 mV/A); a driver fault, a stall, a burst timeout and a
  run time cap each end the run; the encoder self-check ends the run with its named reason. Every exit path stops the
  motor and the encoder. PANIC PROCEDURE IS PHYSICAL SUPPLY DISCONNECT ONLY.
  In the 2a legs (phase 2a): the same current, charge and time guards every SAMPLE_MS, each ending the run; a driver
  fault is a FINDING there (it is what the reference legs measure), recorded, cleared with testResetFault(), and the
  leg climbs no higher in that entry; every measuring window checks the encoder against the driver's hall position
  (bWindowEncOk()) and a disagreement ends the run; no hands-off command passes PK1_CAP_INCR at a row from 12 V up (a
  power-commanded drive reads the increment the library wrote back and ends the run if it does). The test limit is
  2 A in every leg but the ladder at 11.1 V, which needs 3 A (DAT rowLadderA, why there).
  In the 2b legs (phase 2b): the same guards. L-coast changes the fault response and L-offscan the commutation offsets;
  each leg reads what was in force before it, restores it on its one exit whatever ended it, reads it back, and ends
  the run (AR_SETTING) if the restore did not take. L-coast floats the bridge at speed only where the motor's back-EMF
  stays under COAST_EMF_MAX_PM of the told supply (a floated bridge's diodes would otherwise pump a bench supply that
  cannot sink current, plan sec 13): at the 12 V and 24 V rows' tops it is 7.9 V and 9.2 V, so it never binds there.
  In the 2c legs (phase 2c): the same guards, plus L-handload's two charge caps on the STALL charge (the DC link above
  the sheet's no-load ceiling): a step's (HAND_STEP_CAP_MAS) stops that step's motor, the leg's (HAND_LEG_CAP_MAS) ends
  the run; the default-limit step runs only at 12 V, never at 24 V, and only when a whole step's cap is left in the
  leg; it raises the absolute abort to HAND_DEF_ABORT_MA for its own drive only. Every limit, hold and abort a step
  changes is put back on its exit and read back. L-sag commands the 22.2 V row's shipped top, 470e6, past PK1_CAP_INCR
  ON PURPOSE: it is the analysis's fault-first case (P-S7), attended, and optional. STOP MOTOR is live whenever the
  shaft is driven. The run's time cap counts only the time a step runs (runIdleMs: a screen waiting on him is not
  an unwatched motor).
  Task 3686: L-wiring's walk (checkWiring(), the library's own: power 10, one electrical cycle each way, a leg that
  draws more than a healthy walk is ended by shorting the phases) runs under the 2 A test limit before the rest zero
  is read, so no harness guard samples during its ~1.3 s; a walk that does not pass ends the run before anything else
  drives (AR_WIRING). L-power drives as the ladder does: every guard, the row's ladder test limit, bCheckTop().

  RECORD DISCIPLINE (the scan's): tag-first, comma-separated name,value pairs, tags B1- (this binary), BE- (the encoder
  object), SIGNOFF / SIGNOFF-DECL (sf 1, DOCs/plans/VISIT-SIGNOFF-DESIGN.md sec B.1). Every record prints every field in
  the same order; absence is NA. Records are assembled by isp_bench_log and emitted by ONE debug() statement (lineEmit),
  each under 280 bytes. NO debug() runs while the motor is driven: every record of a burst is emitted after it stops,
  and every 2a leg keeps its readings in VAR and emits them once the motor is at rest (the ladder's at its end).
  Directions are named by the INCREMENT SIGN commanded (NEG / POS, as the scan does, PL-19) beside the direction the
  halls MEASURED (RISE / FALL through the order 1-5-4-6-2-3), never by "forward".

  HOW IT IS RUN (tools/bench-run.sh, which adds -D BENCH_CFG and the tier's own symbols)
      tools/bench-run.sh single-measure-v12p0            (every hands-off leg in one run; one tier per Doco voltage)
      tools/bench-run.sh single-qualify-v12p0            (D2: the hands-off qualification in one run; every Doco voltage)
      tools/bench-run.sh single-hallmap-v12p0            (one leg: single-hallmap / -mininc / -ladder / -ramp / -stops;
                                                          single-coast / -offscan at v12p0 and v24p0; single-passprobe)
      tools/bench-run.sh single-passprobe-v12p0 clk-200  (a clock by NAME, as every Doco tier takes)
      tools/bench-run.sh single-handload-v12p0           (attended: single-handload / -heldpush at v12p0 and v24p0;
                                                          the optional single-sag-v22p2 / -v18p5, single-pinch-v18p5)
  Built without -D BENCH_CFG -D BENCH_DOCO (the compile gate's as-written build), it starts nothing: it prints its
  banner and a B1-REFUSE record and ends.
}

' Select the single-motor configuration in isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2 (a -D BENCH_CFG build uses the bench file instead)
#DEFINE CFG_SINGLE_MOTOR
#IFDEF __PNUT_TS__
#PRAGMA EXPORTDEF CFG_SINGLE_MOTOR
#ENDIF

CON { timing }

    CLK_FREQ = 270_000_000                                  ' tools/bench-run.sh sets this line to a clock chosen by NAME
    _clkfreq = CLK_FREQ

CON { build identity }

    SRC_REV     = 6                                         ' hand-bumped whenever this file changes
    FMT_VERSION = 5                                         ' B1- record-format version (5: B1-WIRING, B1-POWER; B1-BUILD wiring/power/qualify; B1-MOTOR2 ke_used; B1-HPUSHR limit_ticks)

CON { the bench this image is built for }

  ' THE DOCO BENCH, -D BENCH_CFG -D BENCH_DOCO -D DOCO_V*: isp_bldc_motor_userconfig_bench.spin2 states it (one motor, its
  '  board READ and EXPECTED to be a Rev A, the encoder pins, the TOLD voltage). Any other build is not the Doco bench:
  '  the values below are then NOT_THE_DOCO_BENCH and main() refuses before it starts anything.
#ifdef BENCH_DOCO
    BUILT_FOR_DOCO  = TRUE
    MOTOR_BASE      = user.ONLY_MOTOR_BASE
    MOTOR_DET_MODE  = user.ONLY_BOARD_TYPE
    EXPECTED_BOARD  = user.EXPECTED_BOARD
    ENC_PIN_A       = user.ENCODER_PIN_A
    ENC_PIN_B       = user.ENCODER_PIN_B
    TOLD_MV         = user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE_TOLD_MV
#else
    BUILT_FOR_DOCO  = FALSE
    NOT_THE_DOCO_BENCH = -1
    MOTOR_BASE      = NOT_THE_DOCO_BENCH
    MOTOR_DET_MODE  = NOT_THE_DOCO_BENCH
    EXPECTED_BOARD  = NOT_THE_DOCO_BENCH
    ENC_PIN_A       = NOT_THE_DOCO_BENCH
    ENC_PIN_B       = NOT_THE_DOCO_BENCH
    TOLD_MV         = NOT_THE_DOCO_BENCH
#endif

CON { the Doco's numbers -- THE ONE PER-MOTOR BLOCK }

  ' EVERY NUMBER HERE BELONGS TO THE MOTOR, and is re-derived for another one. Each line gives its provenance (MEASURED /
  '  DERIVED / MODELED / STEPHEN, doctrine overlay P8) and its 6.5in counterpart where one exists. A change here is a row
  '  in the plan's sec 4 "Edited from the 6.5in instruments" list, made in the same commit.

  ' THE GEOMETRY
    ' 8 poles (DOCs/DOCOMotor.pdf, MEASURED by reading the sheet); 6.5in: 15 pole pairs (test_bench_dual.spin2 ALIGN block)
    MOTOR_POLE_PAIRS        = 4
    ' hall ticks per revolution: the encoder object's own (24, DOCOENG_MOTOR.md); 6.5in: 90 (ALIGN_TICKS_PER_REV)
    HALL_TICKS_PER_REV      = enc.HALL_TICKS_PER_REV
    ' encoder counts per revolution and per hall tick: the encoder object's (1,440 and 60); 6.5in: no encoder
    ENC_COUNTS_PER_REV      = enc.ENC_COUNTS_PER_REV
    ENC_COUNTS_PER_TICK     = enc.COUNTS_PER_HALL_TICK
    ' DERIVED: one electrical cycle is 1,440 / 4 = 360 counts, so ONE ENCODER COUNT IS ONE ELECTRICAL DEGREE on this motor;
    '  a hall boundary every 360 / 6 = 60 counts
    ENC_COUNTS_PER_ECYCLE   = ENC_COUNTS_PER_REV / MOTOR_POLE_PAIRS
    ENC_COUNTS_PER_BOUNDARY = ENC_COUNTS_PER_ECYCLE / wheel.HALL_TICKS_PER_CYCLE
    ' a compile-time check that the three agree (24 = 4 x 6); the compiler stops with "Divide by zero" here when they do not
    GEOMETRY_AGREES         = (HALL_TICKS_PER_REV == MOTOR_POLE_PAIRS * wheel.HALL_TICKS_PER_CYCLE)
    CHECK_GEOMETRY          = 1 / -GEOMETRY_AGREES      ' MOTOR_POLE_PAIRS x 6 is not HALL_TICKS_PER_REV: fix the geometry above

  ' THE RATINGS (DOCs/DOCOMotor.pdf, read 2026-10-03; DOCs/analyses/DOCO-DESK-MODEL-2026-10-03.md sec 1.1)
    ' back-EMF constant, line-to-line peak, mV per 1,000 rpm (the sheet; phase 2's misdial check); 6.5in: none in the instruments
    KE_MV_PER_KRPM          = 3_530
    ' rated current, mA: the sheet's 0.0625 N.m / 0.034 N.m/A (trapezoidal); 2.14 A phase peak sinusoidal (analysis 1.1)
    RATED_MA                = 1_840
    ' no-load current ceiling, mA (the sheet's 0.4 A max)
    NO_LOAD_MA_MAX          = 400

  ' THE PROTECTION (every current in mA; converted to sense mV through the DETECTED board, senseMvPerAmp())
    ' The test current limit, whole amps (testSetCurrentLimits() takes amps): the least that is not under the rated 1.84 A.
    '  MODELED (analysis F9 / P-H2): on Rev A a 2 A limit holds a firm stall to 2.1 A at 12 V and 2.9 A at 24 V, where the
    '  fold's 4 mV floor sets it. 6.5in: the library's I_PEAK_A 40 / I_CONT_A 27, the MOSFETs' (t0-reva lowers them to 2)
    TEST_PEAK_A             = 2
    TEST_CONT_A             = 2
    ' The absolute current abort, mA of DC link, for ABS_ABORT_SAMPLES consecutive samples: 2 x the rated 1.84 A. DERIVED:
    '  with the test limit holding the phase at 2-2.9 A the DC link stays under it, so it fires only if the limiter does not.
    '  On Rev A it is 18.4 mV, six times the +-3 mV per-frame noise (FOLD_MIN_MV's note). 6.5in: test_bench_scan ABS_ABORT_MV
    '  1_500 (10 A at 150 mV/A)
    ABS_ABORT_MA            = 2 * RATED_MA
    ABS_ABORT_SAMPLES       = 4                             ' as the scan's
    ' The run charge cap, mA x s of DC link while driven: one minute at the rated current. DERIVED: the hall map's crawl draws
    '  ~0.02-0.1 A (MODELED, analysis 2.1, 25 % rungs) for under a minute, a hundredth of it; the cap ends a run that keeps
    '  drawing current nothing predicted. Its resolution on Rev A: a zero 0.05 mV off reads 10 mA, 0.6 A.s a minute.
    '  6.5in: test_bench_scan RUN_CHARGE_CAP_MVS 432_000 (0.8 Ah at 150 mV/A)
  '  PHASE 2a: this minute is the BASE of the cap; each 2a leg built (and, phase 2b, each 2b leg) adds the sheet's no-load
  '  ceiling (NO_LOAD_MA_MAX) over its estimated length (RUN_CHARGE_CAP_MAS, CON { legs }). DERIVED: the unloaded model draws 0.02-0.16 A of DC
  '  link (analysis 2.1), the 2023 notes up to 0.89 A at a top for seconds; 0.4 A over a whole leg is above both, and a
  '  run that keeps drawing more than that over its length is drawing current nothing predicted.
    RUN_CHARGE_RATED_S      = 60
    RUN_CHARGE_BASE_MAS     = RATED_MA * RUN_CHARGE_RATED_S

  ' THE HALL-MAP LEG'S CRAWL (L-hallmap). Two rungs, named by their hall-tick rate, each converted to a driver increment at
  '  run time by the drive law (hallMapIncrement()). DERIVED: 24 ticks/s is one revolution a second (60 rpm), 96 is four
  '  (240 rpm): 3 % and 13 % of the lowest Rev A ceiling (7.4 V, 754 ticks/s), and 16 x / 66 x the shipped "anything below
  '  yields NO rotation" 544_628. Two speeds separate what is geometry (the same at both) from what is timing (grows with
  '  speed). 6.5in: test_bench_scan LOW_SPEED_INCRE 18_375_000 (49 ticks/s, the walking rung)
    HALLMAP_SLOW_TPS        = 24
    HALLMAP_FAST_TPS        = 96
    ' One burst crosses BURST_SPAN_TICKS edges after its first: exactly BURST_REVS revolutions, so both ends of the self-check
    '  span are the same hall boundary. 49 edges and the stop's few more fit the encoder's 64-entry ring, so no record is
    '  emitted while the motor turns. 6.5in: WIN_TICKS_LOW 90 (one wheel revolution)
    BURST_REVS              = 2
    BURST_SPAN_TICKS        = BURST_REVS * HALL_TICKS_PER_REV
    BURST_SPAN_EDGES        = BURST_SPAN_TICKS + 1
    BURST_MAP_EDGES         = BURST_SPAN_TICKS              ' edges 0 .. 47 go into the map: one per boundary per revolution
    BURSTS_PER_SET          = 2                             ' so a set holds SECTOR_REVS revolutions
    SECTOR_REVS             = BURSTS_PER_SET * BURST_REVS
    ' No hall edge for this long while driven is a stall. DERIVED: the slow rung's edge interval is 42 ms; from rest the
    '  first edge comes after the built-in ramp, ~0.3 s. 6.5in: ALIGN_STALL_MS 120_000 (a hand turn, not a drive)
    HALLMAP_STALL_MS        = 1_000

  ' ---- PHASE 2a: the hands-off measuring legs ----

  ' THE ROWS. The shipped Rev A Doco table this harness measures today's behaviour against, MIRRORED in DAT rowMv /
  '  rowCeilIncr / rowLadderA (below, "the Doco's rows") from isp_bldc_motor.spin2 confgurePowerLimits() (:5418-5419):
  '  the instrument places its rungs before the first drive, and the library has no getter for its ceiling. The legs that
  '  command by power read back the increment the library wrote (testGetDriveFollow()) and print it beside the mirror
  '  (B1-RAMP lib_incr), so a stale mirror shows in the first such record. 6.5in: one measured ceiling scaled by the
  '  voltage (HUB_CEIL_INCR_AT_NOMINAL); the 6.5in instruments chose their own rungs.
    ROW_COUNT               = 7
    ' the shipped reverse minimum, "anything below yields NO rotation" (:5421); the forward sign's is 1 (0 - VALUE_NOT_SET,
    '  PL-71). L-mininc runs it as one of its rungs. 6.5in: HUB_FLOOR_INCR 100_000 (Visit 9 E4)
    SHIPPED_MIN_INCR        = 544_628

  ' PK-1 (analysis F3, sec 5.2 row D1): one drive pass's field step passes the LAG_HOLD-to-fault margin (25 counts) above
  '  419.4e6 on this motor (2,806 rpm), where a disturbance faults instead of slipping. DERIVED, exact. No hands-off
  '  command passes PK1_CAP_INCR at a row from PK1_CAP_FROM_MV up (the arbiter's 2a ruling: "at 12-24 V ... never past
  '  419e6"): the 22.2 V row's top runs at 419e6 (power 89), not its shipped 470e6. 11.1 V's shipped top, 545e6, is
  '  P-S2's own measurement (the model predicts its climb faults near 3,000-3,200 rpm) and runs uncapped; 7.4 V's, 282e6,
  '  is under the cap. 6.5in: none (its top field step is 12.8 counts, analysis 5.1)
    PK1_CAP_INCR            = 419_000_000
    PK1_CAP_FROM_MV         = 12_000

  ' THE LADDER (L-ladder). Rungs at DAT ladderPcts (25, 50, 75, 100) % of the row's shipped ceiling, a rung over the cap
  '  run at the cap; then, at a capped row, each DAT ladderExtIncr rung (360e6, 400e6) above the ceiling and not past the
  '  cap -- the analysis's "add rungs up to 400e6" (L2), toward the duty reserve (P-S3: 12 V's top runs 71-76 % duty). The
  '  100 % rung is the row's CEILING (R23-SGL-SMOOTH). 6.5in: test_bench_dual's LADDER and the scan's own speeds
    LADDER_PCT_COUNT        = 4
    LADDER_EXT_COUNT        = 2
    LADDER_MAX_RUNGS        = LADDER_PCT_COUNT + LADDER_EXT_COUNT
    LADDER_CEIL_RUNG        = LADDER_PCT_COUNT - 1
    ' the misdial check's fit: at least this many clean rungs, spanning at least this fraction of the fastest one's speed
    '  (per mille). DERIVED: two points fit any line; three expose a bad one; half the range keeps the slope's error under
    '  the 3 % the check judges when each duty is good to 1 %
    MISDIAL_MIN_POINTS      = 3
    MISDIAL_MIN_SPAN_PM     = 500
    ' THE RESERVE CEILING (B1-FFLINE): the increment where the duty line reaches DUTY_RESERVE_PM of the drive's duty ceiling
    '  -- the 6.5in's reserve, CARRIED UNCHANGED (ADDING_MOTOR.md step 6, "about 7 % in hand"; 165e6 ran at 92-93 %
    '  MEASURED, Visit 8b/9; the analysis's doco_top() uses 0.925): the same rule, so the two motors' ceilings compare
    DUTY_RESERVE_PM         = 925

  ' THE MISDIAL CHECK (R23-SGL-MISDIAL). The duty line's slope against the encoder's speed predicts the supply from the
  '  sheet's back-EMF constant (KE_MV_PER_KRPM above) through the drive's duty-to-volts scale: the phase voltage's peak is
  '  Vbus x duty / (DUTY_VOLT_DIV x frame_cnt) (MODELED: DOCs/plans/servo-model/spin2_model.py:521, Vbus x duty / (16 x
  '  3_068), 3_068 = frame_cnt / 2 at 270 MHz; the model's 6.5in ladder fit rests on it). Its tolerance is DERIVED from the
  '  sheet and D1's first run (plan sec 4). UNFITTED (KE_IS_FITTED FALSE): the sheet's +-10 % on Ke (its no-load speed,
  '  6,800 +-10 %) plus the +-3 % residual (the lead and R x iq, analysis sec 8 L2) -- +-13 %, which catches a gross misdial
  '  (12 V told, 18.5 or 7.4 set) and not an adjacent row; FITTED: +-3 %, which separates adjacent rows (12 / 11.1 V and
  '  24 / 22.2 V lie 7.5-8 % apart). WHEN EACH APPLIES (arbiter decision D5): there is no rebuild in the middle of a visit.
  '  D1 runs this build, KE_IS_FITTED FALSE, judging +-130 per mille in the run; the D1 EVALUATION fits Ke across the rows
  '  and applies the fitted +-30 per mille OFFLINE to each row's logged raw ratio (B1-MISDIAL ratio_ppm, vpred_mv, and the
  '  inputs to refit Ke: slope_e9, frame_cnt, ke_mv_krpm, told_mv; B1-MOTOR's cpr and duty_volt_div); the D2 build
  '  (task 3686: -D SINGLE_QUALIFY, the single-qualify tiers) sets KE_IS_FITTED TRUE and predicts from
  '  KE_FITTED_MV_PER_KRPM. 6.5in: none (its pack was sensed)
#ifdef SINGLE_QUALIFY
    KE_IS_FITTED            = TRUE
#else
    KE_IS_FITTED            = FALSE
#endif
    KE_SHEET_TOL_PCT        = 10
    ' THE FITTED Ke, mV per 1,000 rpm, line-to-line peak: PROVISIONAL, the sheet's 3,530 until D1's EVALUATION fits it
    '  across the rows (arbiter decision D5) and sets it here, before the D2 pack is built. A D2 build left at the sheet's
    '  value judges +-30 per mille against a Ke that may be off the sheet by up to its 10 %: a correct motor whose Ke is
    '  5 % under the sheet then reads -50 and FAILS (the 3686 desk model) -- so this number is a D2 precondition
    KE_FITTED_MV_PER_KRPM   = 3_530
    ' the Ke the misdial check predicts from: the sheet's (KE_MV_PER_KRPM) unfitted, KE_FITTED_MV_PER_KRPM fitted (TRUE is -1)
    KE_USED_MV_PER_KRPM     = KE_MV_PER_KRPM + (-KE_IS_FITTED) * (KE_FITTED_MV_PER_KRPM - KE_MV_PER_KRPM)
    DUTY_VOLT_DIV           = 8

  ' THE MINIMUM INCREMENT (L-mininc, PL-71). A descending sweep of crawl rates, DAT minincTpsX100 (hall ticks/s x 100):
  '  24, 12, 6, 4, 3, 2, the shipped minimum's own increment (1.46 ticks/s), 1, 0.75, 0.6. DERIVED: from the hall map's
  '  slow rung, past the shipped minimum, to where one electrical cycle (360 counts, MININC_WIN_COUNTS) takes 10 s
  '  (MININC_MAX_WIN_MS) -- a window at least a cycle long sees every sector of the field's pattern. 6.5in: Visit 9 E4's
  '  rungs from 544_628 down to 100_000 (0.27 ticks/s of 90 a revolution), each "rotated at exactly its commanded rate"
    MININC_RUNGS            = 10
    MININC_SHIPPED_RUNG     = -1                            ' the DAT entry that means SHIPPED_MIN_INCR
    ' STEADY, from the encoder: the window's travel within MININC_SYNC_TOL_COUNTS of the field's commanded travel -- a
    '  quarter of an electrical cycle; a rotor that slips a pole pair reads a whole cycle (360 counts) short -- and every one
    '  of MININC_SUBWINS equal sub-windows advancing the window's way by at least MININC_SUB_MIN_PCT % of its share of the
    '  commanded travel (no stall or stutter inside the window). DERIVED from the geometry: 1 count = 1 electrical degree
    MININC_WIN_COUNTS       = ENC_COUNTS_PER_ECYCLE
    MININC_SYNC_TOL_COUNTS  = ENC_COUNTS_PER_ECYCLE / 4
    MININC_SUBWINS          = 4
    MININC_SUB_MIN_PCT      = 50

  ' THE TOP AND THE CRAWL (L-ramp, L-stops). The power-commanded legs drive at the row's TOP POWER: 100 (the shipped
  '  ceiling), or at a capped row whose ceiling passes PK1_CAP_INCR the largest power whose increment stays under it,
  '  computed from the mirrored ceiling (topPowerFor(): 89 at 22.2 V, which the library maps to 417.8e6 either sign). The
  '  crawl is STOPS_CRAWL_POWER, 30-42 ticks/s by the rows' tables (4/99 of the ceiling). 6.5in: test_bench_t0 T0-25's
  '  power 15 (~59 ticks/s of 90)
    STOPS_CRAWL_POWER       = 5

  ' THE STOP LIMITS (L-stops, L8). stopAfterRotation() armed at rest, in hall ticks (DRU_HALL_TICKS): at the top, DAT
  '  stopTopTicks 7_200 and 9_600 (300 and 400 revolutions: past the top's ramp up and stop at every row, 122 (7.4 V) to
  '  443 (11.1 V) revolutions, DERIVED from analysis sec 6, so most rows cruise first); at the crawl, DAT stopCrawlTicks 24
  '  and 120 (1 and 5 revolutions). stopAfterTime(): STOPS_TOP_MS 15_000 at the top (past every row's ramp up and stop
  '  but 11.1 V's, which stops mid-climb), STOPS_CRAWL_MS 3_000 at the crawl. 6.5in: test_bench_t0 T0_25_ROT_TURNS 1 (90
  '  ticks), T0_25_PLAN_ROT_C 2, T0_25_PLAN_MS_C 1_500
    STOPS_ROT_COUNT         = 2
    STOPS_TOP_MS            = 15_000
    STOPS_CRAWL_MS          = 3_000

  ' THE REST, from the encoder (R23-SGL-STOPROT, -STOPTIME): the shaft is at rest once its count has stayed within
  '  REST_JITTER_COUNTS for REST_QUIET_MS; its rest INSTANT is the first reading already within REST_JITTER_COUNTS of the
  '  final count. DERIVED: the built-in deceleration (638 rpm/s, 15,313 counts/s^2 on 1,440 counts) moves the shaft one
  '  count in the last 46 ms of a stop (the S-curve's tail, J t^3 / 6), so the shaft's rest is resolved to ~50 ms, never
  '  to the few milliseconds the field's own stop is. 6.5in: none (the hub has no shaft angle)
    REST_JITTER_COUNTS      = 1
    REST_QUIET_MS           = 300

  ' ---- PHASE 2b: the coast-down, the offset scan, the pass-period probe ----

  ' THE ROWS L-COAST AND L-OFFSCAN RUN AT: DAT rowL13 (the analysis's sec 8 L1 and L3 name the 12 V and 24 V rows); at
  '  another row each prints B1-LEGSKIP and drives nothing. THE SPEEDS: DAT speedPcts, 25, 50 and 100 % of the row's
  '  ceiling, capped at its top (the analysis's L1 / L3 stimulus; at 12 V 559 / 1,119 / 2,238 rpm, at 24 V 653 / 1,306 /
  '  2,612 rpm). 6.5in: the scan's QTR and HALF rungs, RATE_QTR_EXPECTED 98 and RATE_HALF_EXPECTED 196 ticks/s
    SPEED_PCT_COUNT         = 3
    SPEED_TOP_IDX           = SPEED_PCT_COUNT - 1          ' the 100 % speed: the coast cell's and the lead check's top

  ' THE COAST (L-coast, the analysis's L1). Steady at the speed (arrived, LADDER_SETTLE_MS, a COAST_STEADY_MS window: the
  '  speed it coasts from and the DC link that, with Kt, gives the friction torque and so J), then
  '  setFaultResponse(FR_SHIPPED, 0) with holdAtStop(FALSE) makes the guarded testForceFault() FLOAT the bridge, and the
  '  encoder is read every COAST_SAMPLE_US until the shaft rests (REST_JITTER_COUNTS for REST_QUIET_MS). DERIVED: the coast
  '  lasts 65-738 ms from 2,238 rpm (analysis sec 8 L1; this file's desk numbers, sgl2b_numbers.py, task 3679), so the
  '  analysis's ">= 2 kHz" puts 130-1,476 readings on it; COAST_MAX_SAMPLES holds 2 s of them, 2.4 x the longest the
  '  bracket allows anywhere (834 ms, 24 V's top). A coast not at rest in COAST_WAIT_MAX_MS is recorded as such and the
  '  shaft stopped. 6.5in: none (the fault study's coasts were judged on the halls, test_bench_dual FLTRESP)
    COAST_SAMPLE_US         = 500
    COAST_MAX_SAMPLES       = 4_000
    COAST_WAIT_MAX_MS       = 3_000
    COAST_STEADY_MS         = 2_000
    ' the forced fault must read DCS_FAULTED this soon after testForceFault() returns: the driver takes it on its next
    '  driven frame, one drive pass (0.52 ms) after the front cog's ~1 ms answer (isp_bldc_motor.spin2 testForceFault())
    COAST_FAULT_WAIT_MS     = 50
    ' B1-COASTPT: a reading is printed when the shaft has moved 1 / COAST_PTS_MAX of the coast's travel since the last one
    '  printed, or COAST_EMIT_GAP_MS has passed: under ~70 records a coast, dense in time where the shaft slows
    COAST_PTS_MAX           = 48
    COAST_EMIT_GAP_MS       = 50
    ' THE REGEN GUARD: a floated bridge's body diodes conduct into the supply once the back-EMF (line-to-line peak, Ke x
    '  rpm) reaches it, and a bench supply cannot sink current (plan sec 13). A coast speed whose back-EMF reaches this
    '  share of the told supply is SKIPPED. DERIVED: 7.9 V of 12 (66 %) and 9.2 V of 24 (38 %) at the two rows' tops
    COAST_EMF_MAX_PM        = 900
    ' R23-SGL-COAST's bound per row: DAT coastLoMs / coastHiMs, the coast from the row's 100 % speed at the bracket's two
    '  corners, (J / Bv) ln(1 + Bv w / Tc) (analysis sec 1.2: shortest J 2e-6, Tc 0.006, Bv 1.05e-5; longest J 8e-6, Tc
    '  0.002, Bv 5e-6): 12 V 65.5 .. 737.9 ms, 24 V 74.5 .. 833.8. The upper rounded up; the lower rounded down less the
    '  reader's own resolution, 2.9 ms -- the rest instant is the last reading the count moved past REST_JITTER_COUNTS,
    '  so it reads early by the last ~2 counts' time, 2.4 ms at the shortest corner's deceleration, plus a reading's
    '  0.5 ms (sgl2b_model.py reads that corner 66 and 73 ms): 62 .. 738 and 71 .. 834. PER-MOTOR: the bracket is the
    '  Doco's; MODELED, not measured

  ' THE OFFSET SCAN (L-offscan, the analysis's L3; test_bench_scan's method at the Doco's numbers). Per sign and speed the
  '  offset that sign uses (offset_fwd for NEG increments, offset_rev for POS: testSetFwdRevIndep()) is stepped
  '  OFS_STEP_DEG at a time from the shipped one out to OFS_SPAN_DEG, one SIDE at a time (+ then -), each side entered
  '  from rest at the shipped pair, so no step is larger than OFS_STEP_DEG while driven; each side's first point (the
  '  shipped offset) is its reference, the two references show the drift. Each point: OFS_SETTLE_MS, then OFS_WINDOW_MS
  '  averaged: the DC link through the detected board (Rev A resolves a 5 s mean to ~10 mA; one 5 ms reading is +-3 mV,
  '  600 mA), duty, err, held passes, following, and the hall zero at that speed from every captured edge. DERIVED from
  '  the scan: 6.5in COARSE_STEP_DEG 10, FINE_STEP_DEG 5, HARD_LIMIT_DEG 90 (test_bench_scan.spin2:587-590), SETTLE_MS 1,000
  '  (:508), windows in ticks (WIN_TICKS_FINE 270, :521); the analysis's L3 asks 5 degree steps over +-30
    OFS_STEP_DEG            = 5
    OFS_SPAN_DEG            = 30
    OFS_SIDE_POINTS         = OFS_SPAN_DEG / OFS_STEP_DEG + 1   ' 7 a side: 0, 5, ... 30
    OFS_SIDES               = 2
    OFS_POINTS              = OFS_SIDES * OFS_SIDE_POINTS        ' 14 a speed and sign
    OFS_SETTLE_MS           = 1_000
    OFS_WINDOW_MS           = 5_000
    ' THE POINT ABORT (the scan's, in mA through the detected board): a point whose DC link stays over its side's
    '  reference x OFS_POINT_X100 / 100 for OFS_POINT_SAMPLES readings, or over OFS_CEIL_MA for ABS_ABORT_SAMPLES, has met
    '  the current wall: the side ends there (RO_WALL), as the scan's walk does. 6.5in: POINT_ABORT_X100 250,
    '  POINT_ABORT_CEIL_PCT 80 of ABS_ABORT_MV, POINT_ABORT_SAMPLES 40 (test_bench_scan.spin2:645-654). The Doco adds a
    '  floor, OFS_POINT_FLOOR_MA, the sheet's no-load ceiling: a 2.5 x of an unloaded reference near 0.05 A would sit
    '  inside one Rev A reading's noise
    OFS_POINT_X100          = 250
    OFS_POINT_SAMPLES       = 40
    OFS_CEIL_MA             = ABS_ABORT_MA * 80 / 100           ' 2_944
    OFS_POINT_FLOOR_MA      = NO_LOAD_MA_MAX
    ' THE MINIMUM: least squares of a parabola in the offset over the speed's clean points (DONE, no re-sync, following
    '  within FOLLOW_TOL_PM), for the DC link (the current minimum: the magnet reference for Z, arbiter decision D2) and,
    '  beside it, for duty. RESOLVED when at least OFS_FIT_MIN_PTS points, the curvature positive, the vertex inside the
    '  scanned span, and the VERTEX'S OWN standard error (the residual's, carried through -b / 2a by the inverse normal
    '  matrix) at most OFS_VERT_SE_MAX_X10. DERIVED (sgl2b_model.py): a rule on the curvature's significance alone (2 standard
    '  errors) let 22 of 400 noisy unloaded 25 % fits through with vertices anywhere in +-30, each a false lead-check FAIL;
    '  2.5 degrees keeps two vertices' difference inside the 10 degree bound at ~3 standard errors. 6.5in: FIT_MIN_PTS 6 /
    '  CONFIRM_MIN_PTS 5, the FIT_POOR_* rules (test_bench_scan.spin2:625-635)
    OFS_FIT_MIN_PTS         = 5
    OFS_VERT_SE_MAX_X10     = 25

  ' THE PASS-PERIOD PROBE (L-passprb, plan sec 1.4). Each sign at PASSPRB_PCT of the row's ceiling (capped): settle, then a
  '  window of at least PASSPRB_WIN_MS by getms(); its time is summed from each reading's getct() step as whole seconds and
  '  a remainder of clocks (never one getct() difference: signed, it wraps after 2^31 clocks, 6.1 s at 350 MHz); the
  '  encoder's travel over it against |incr| x 360 counts per electrical cycle x the pass rate of the ACTUAL frame,
  '  clkfreq / (frame_cnt x DRIVE_PASS_FRAMES) (testGetDriveConstants()), in ppm. DERIVED: 10 s at 1,119 rpm is 268,560
  '  counts, 4 ppm a count; the frame's own rounding moves the pass rate -267 .. +125 ppm from 44 kHz / 23 across the clock
  '  names (sgl2b_numbers.py), which is why the actual frame is the reference. 6.5in: none (test_bench_dual's CLOCK part
  '  judged the frame and pass from the driver's own counters, expectedPassUs())
    PASSPRB_PCT             = 50
    PASSPRB_WIN_MS          = 10_000

  ' THE COLD BACK-EMF Z IS NOT BUILT (plan sec 4: "attempted only if the Doco's back-EMF at hand speed clears the align
  '  instrument's clip band"). DERIVED (sgl2b_numbers.py): (1) A HAND SPIN CANNOT HOLD A SPEED: at the bracket's longest
  '  coast a shaft flicked to 300 rpm rests in 121 ms after 0.30 revolution (60 rpm: 25 ms, 0.01 rev), and the align leg
  '  needs ALIGN_TURNS 3 revolutions at a held speed (test_bench_dual.spin2:1837). (2) THE SIGNAL: the Doco makes 1 / 4.7
  '  of the 6.5in's volts per electrical Hz (ke 0.00487 against <= 0.0229 V s/rad, phase peak); the 6.5in's coasting
  '  wheel read 281-1,006 mV p-p at the pins over 17.8-53.4 Hz (MOTOR-6.5IN-TECHNICAL-MANUAL.md sec 4.6, Rev B), so IF Rev A's
  '  phase scale were Rev B's -- NOT ESTABLISHED (VISIT-7C-PASS2-EVALUATION.md sec 8) -- the Doco would swing 3.4-4.0 mV
  '  p-p per electrical Hz, clearing the align's crossing band (bias +- the stray + ALIGN_HYST_MARGIN_MV 4: +-7 mV, 17-27
  '  measured on re-taken legs) only above 52-242 rpm HELD, inside its 20 / 3,200 mV clip (ALIGN_CLIP_LO_MV / _HI_MV,
  '  :1853-1854). With (1) no such speed exists. The encoder Z (L-hallmap, L-offscan) and the current minimum stand.

  ' ---- PHASE 2c: the attended legs (the analysis's sec 8 L5, L6, and the optional L4, L2b) ----

  ' THE ROWS THE ATTENDED LEGS RUN AT: DAT rowL56 (L-handload, L-heldpush: the analysis's L5 and L6 name 12 V and 24 V),
  '  rowHandDef (the default-limit step: 12 V ONLY -- analysis sec 4.1, a firm stall at the default limits reaches 8.8 A
  '  of phase at 12 V and 16.8 A at 24 V, 4 x and 8 x the 2.14 A rating, so NEVER at 24 V), sagIncr / sagExpectFault
  '  (L-sag: 22.2 V and 18.5 V) and pinchIncr (L-pinch: 18.5 V). At another row each leg prints B1-LEGSKIP, drives
  '  nothing, and the panel says so. 6.5in: none (the 6.5in's hand tests ran on wheels: T0-24, floor-grab)

  ' THE HAND LOAD (L-handload, the analysis's L5, P-H1 .. P-H3). The shaft is driven at HAND_POWER from rest (the user's
  '  driveAtPower(), the API path a hand meets), one way, and the operator slows it by hand to a stall. DAT handLimitA
  '  gives each step's test limit, whole amps: 4, 2, then 0 = the library's default (I_PEAK_A / I_CONT_A, the
  '  MOSFETs'). MODELED (analysis 4.1, docohand): power 10 is 207 rpm at 12 V and 241 at 24 V; a firm grip at 4 A holds
  '  the stall to 2.8-2.9 A of phase, at 2 A 2.1-2.9 A, at the default 8.75 A (12 V). 6.5in: floor-grab's LOAD power
  '  and the obstacle's BLK_POWER 7 (test_bench_dual.spin2:16664) at BLK_LIMIT_A 2
    HAND_POWER              = 10
    ' THE GRIP: the encoder's speed (the 35 ms arrival ring) under this share of the commanded speed is his hand on the
    '  shaft. DERIVED: an unloaded crawl follows at 100 % (P-S1); half is past any following error and any cogging
    '  ripple, and well before a stall. 6.5in: none (the obstacle was met by the halls' stand)
    HAND_CONTACT_PM         = 500
    ' bounds: from AT_SPEED to his grip, and the whole ACT. DERIVED: the panel says when to grip; half a minute to read
    '  it and reach the shaft; a minute bounds a creeping grip under a test limit (the default step is bounded by the
    '  stand and its step cap instead)
    HAND_GRIP_WAIT_MS       = 30_000
    HAND_ACT_MAX_MS         = 60_000
    ' THE STALL CHARGE: the DC link ABOVE the sheet's no-load ceiling (NO_LOAD_MA_MAX), integrated while driven: what a
    '  load adds. A step's cap stops that step's motor; the leg's cap ends the run. DERIVED from the analysis's sec 4.1
    '  table, MODELED with a 100 ms rise from the grip and the shaft standing 150 ms after it (sgl2c_model.py part 2a): the
    '  default limit's firm stall draws 4.6-6.1 A of DC link at 12 V and reaches its latch with 4.6-6.3 A.s used, under
    '  7.7; at 24 V it draws 8.2-12.3 A and trips the cap 0.70-1.04 s after the grip, BEFORE the latch (1.16 s) -- the
    '  plan's sec 4.1 leg cap (never needed: 24 V never runs the default step). The test limits' stalls (0.40-0.79 A) use
    '  at most 0.42 A.s. The leg's cap is two default steps' (the step and one redo); the default step runs only while a
    '  whole step's cap is left in the leg ("only if the leg charge cap allows", the dispatch). 6.5in: none (its 432 A.s
    '  run cap only)
    HAND_STEP_CAP_MAS       = 7_700
    HAND_LEG_CAP_MAS        = 2 * HAND_STEP_CAP_MAS
    HAND_DEF_NEED_MAS       = HAND_STEP_CAP_MAS
    ' THE DEFAULT STEP'S ABSOLUTE ABORT, mA of DC link: ABS_ABORT_MA (3,680) would trip a 12 V firm stall at the default
    '  limit (4.6-6.1 A) in 20 ms, before the stop it measures. DERIVED: 8 A is 31 % over that stall's top and the 24 V
    '  stall's bottom (8.2 A) -- the 24 V case it would also stop, were it ever run. 40 mV on Rev A. For that step's
    '  drive only; every other drive keeps ABS_ABORT_MA
    HAND_DEF_ABORT_MA       = 8_000

  ' THE HELD STOP (L-heldpush, the analysis's L6, P-H4). The hold at the library's defaults (wheel.HOLD_CEILING_PCT 10,
  '  HOLD_RISE_MS 250, HOLD_LIMIT_MS 10_000, HOLD_SLIP_TICKS 2 -- referenced, never copied), armed fresh for each step
  '  as T0-24 arms it (T0_24_REARM_MS 20: the stop mode floated long enough for the front cog to read HS_OFF, then
  '  SM_BRAKE again). DERIVED (analysis 4.2): on the Doco one hall tick is 15 degrees of shaft, so the hold's duty
  '  stays at duty_min until the push crosses the first hall edge (0-15 degrees from where it rested), rises to its
  '  ceiling over 250 ms displaced -- 22 mN.m at 12 V, 44 at 24 V -- and slips at the second edge (15-30 degrees).
  '  6.5in: T0-24's HOLD-RISE / HOLD-SLIP rows (test_bench_t0.spin2:1117-1138), one tick 4 degrees of wheel
    HELD_REARM_MS           = 20
    HELD_SETTLE_MS          = 300
    ' the sensor that sees him finish: after the hold gave way (HS_SLIPPED) or let go (HS_LIMITED), the encoder still
    '  (REST_JITTER_COUNTS) this long -- he has let go. DERIVED: a slow hand moves a count every ~10 ms, a held shaft
    '  none; a second is unmistakable and short
    HELD_RELEASE_MS         = 1_000
    ' bounds: no turn at all this long ends the step (NOT MEASURED), and the whole ACT
    HELD_WAIT_MS            = 60_000
    HELD_ACT_MAX_MS         = 120_000
    ' a turn the encoder SEES: more than this many counts from where the shaft rested (an eighth of a tick, ~2 degrees)
    HELD_TURN_COUNTS        = ENC_COUNTS_PER_TICK / 8

  ' THE SAG (L-sag, the analysis's L4, P-S7; OPTIONAL, arbiter decision D4). At the row's DAT sagIncr -- the 22.2 V
  '  row's shipped top 470e6, ON PURPOSE past PK1_CAP_INCR (its field step, 28.0 counts a pass, passes the 25-count
  '  LAG_HOLD-to-fault margin: the analysis's fault-first case), and the 18.5 V row's 398e6 (23.7 counts, under it:
  '  the slip-first case) -- he dials the supply down ~1 V/s. "SPEED LOST": the encoder's speed under SAG_LOST_PM of
  '  the command for SAG_LOST_MS, or a fault (or a re-sync), whichever comes first. DERIVED: the analysis's own mark of
  '  a slip is "field 2 % under command" (sec 5.3 table); 50 ms is ten readings, past the 35 ms ring's own lag.
  '  6.5in: none (its pack was never dialled during a run)
    SAG_LOST_PM             = 980
    SAG_LOST_MS             = 50
    SAG_WAIT_MS             = 120_000                       ' from AT_SPEED: 22.2 V down to 8 V at 1 V/s is 14 s
    SAG_SETTLE_MS           = 1_000
    SAG_TRACE_MS            = 100                           ' B1-SAGPT: one reading every 100 ms, the last SAG_TRACE_MAX
    SAG_TRACE_MAX           = 256

  ' THE PINCH (L-pinch, the analysis's L2b, P-S8; OPTIONAL as L-sag). At the 18.5 V row's top (398e6, under the PK-1
  '  margin) the unloaded DC link over PINCH_IDLE_MS is the reference; "LOAD SEEN" is a 100 ms mean (PINCH_MEAN_N
  '  readings) PINCH_SEEN_MA over it, "LOAD GONE" back under half that for PINCH_GONE_MS. DERIVED: Rev A's +-3 mV is
  '  +-600 mA a reading; twenty readings' mean is about +-130 mA, so 300 mA is a load, not noise (status only: the
  '  records carry the trace, and nothing is judged -- the load's torque is not measured, so no cell can be)
    PINCH_IDLE_MS           = 2_000
    PINCH_MEAN_N            = 20
    PINCH_SEEN_MA           = 300
    PINCH_GONE_MS           = 200
    PINCH_WAIT_MS           = 60_000
    PINCH_TRACE_MS          = 20                            ' B1-PINCHPT: one 20 ms mean, the last PINCH_TRACE_MAX
    PINCH_TRACE_MAX         = 256

  ' ---- TASK 3686: the D2 qualification (plan sec 7) ----

  ' THE POWER RUNGS (L-power). driveAtPower() -- the user's path -- at DAT powerPcts, each capped at the row's top power
  '  (rowTopPower: 100, or 89 at 22.2 V, where 100 would pass PK1_CAP_INCR), each power sign, each from rest on the
  '  built-in ramp, then LADDER_SETTLE_MS and a LADDER_WINDOW_MS window, as the ladder's rungs; under the row's ladder
  '  test limit (DAT rowLadderA: 11.1 V's 75 % rung needs 2.57 A). DERIVED: the arbiter's D7 left the ladder commanding
  '  by increment, so the power path's rungs are their own leg; the quarters of the power range are the ladder's
  '  quarters of the ceiling as the library maps them (the row's minimum at power 1 to the ceiling at 100). 6.5in: the
  '  spin legs' and the LIMITS part's POWERMAP powers (test_bench_dual), on the halls
    POWER_RUNG_COUNT        = 4
    POWER_SIGNS             = 2                             ' 0: + power, 1: - power (the API's own sign; the increment's prints beside)
    POWER_SLOTS             = POWER_SIGNS * POWER_RUNG_COUNT

CON { legs -- what this image carries }

  ' Each -D SINGLE_PART_* compiles one leg in; main() runs every leg compiled in, in this order.
#ifdef SINGLE_PART_HALLMAP
    PART_HALLMAP_BUILT = TRUE
#else
    PART_HALLMAP_BUILT = FALSE
#endif
#ifdef SINGLE_PART_MININC
    PART_MININC_BUILT  = TRUE
#else
    PART_MININC_BUILT  = FALSE
#endif
#ifdef SINGLE_PART_LADDER
    PART_LADDER_BUILT  = TRUE
#else
    PART_LADDER_BUILT  = FALSE
#endif
#ifdef SINGLE_PART_RAMP
    PART_RAMP_BUILT    = TRUE
#else
    PART_RAMP_BUILT    = FALSE
#endif
#ifdef SINGLE_PART_STOPS
    PART_STOPS_BUILT   = TRUE
#else
    PART_STOPS_BUILT   = FALSE
#endif
#ifdef SINGLE_PART_COAST
    PART_COAST_BUILT   = TRUE
#else
    PART_COAST_BUILT   = FALSE
#endif
#ifdef SINGLE_PART_OFFSCAN
    PART_OFFSCAN_BUILT = TRUE
#else
    PART_OFFSCAN_BUILT = FALSE
#endif
#ifdef SINGLE_PART_PASSPROBE
    PART_PASSPRB_BUILT = TRUE
#else
    PART_PASSPRB_BUILT = FALSE
#endif
  ' phase 2c, the attended legs: each is its own tier, and any of them builds the panel and the measure cog
  '  (SINGLE_ATTENDED, defined below, compiles their bodies in; an unattended image carries none of them, DBG-16)
#ifdef SINGLE_PART_HANDLOAD
    PART_HANDLOAD_BUILT = TRUE
#ifndef SINGLE_ATTENDED
#define SINGLE_ATTENDED
#endif
#else
    PART_HANDLOAD_BUILT = FALSE
#endif
#ifdef SINGLE_PART_HELDPUSH
    PART_HELDPUSH_BUILT = TRUE
#ifndef SINGLE_ATTENDED
#define SINGLE_ATTENDED
#endif
#else
    PART_HELDPUSH_BUILT = FALSE
#endif
#ifdef SINGLE_PART_SAG
    PART_SAG_BUILT     = TRUE
#ifndef SINGLE_ATTENDED
#define SINGLE_ATTENDED
#endif
#else
    PART_SAG_BUILT     = FALSE
#endif
#ifdef SINGLE_PART_PINCH
    PART_PINCH_BUILT   = TRUE
#ifndef SINGLE_ATTENDED
#define SINGLE_ATTENDED
#endif
#else
    PART_PINCH_BUILT   = FALSE
#endif
  ' task 3686, the D2 qualification's own legs (single-qualify chains them with L-ladder, L-ramp and L-stops)
#ifdef SINGLE_PART_WIRING
    PART_WIRING_BUILT  = TRUE
#else
    PART_WIRING_BUILT  = FALSE
#endif
#ifdef SINGLE_PART_POWER
    PART_POWER_BUILT   = TRUE
#else
    PART_POWER_BUILT   = FALSE
#endif
#ifdef SINGLE_QUALIFY
    QUALIFY_BUILT      = TRUE                               ' the D2 build: the misdial check on the fitted Ke
#else
    QUALIFY_BUILT      = FALSE
#endif
    PART_2A_BUILT      = PART_MININC_BUILT or PART_LADDER_BUILT or PART_RAMP_BUILT or PART_STOPS_BUILT
    PART_2B_BUILT      = PART_COAST_BUILT or PART_OFFSCAN_BUILT or PART_PASSPRB_BUILT
    PART_2C_BUILT      = PART_HANDLOAD_BUILT or PART_HELDPUSH_BUILT or PART_SAG_BUILT or PART_PINCH_BUILT
    PART_Q_BUILT       = PART_WIRING_BUILT or PART_POWER_BUILT
    PART_ANY_BUILT     = PART_HALLMAP_BUILT or PART_2A_BUILT or PART_2B_BUILT or PART_2C_BUILT or PART_Q_BUILT

  ' Each leg's length, s, ESTIMATED (DERIVED from its own stimulus at the built-in rates, analysis sec 6; the worst row):
  '  HALLMAP  8 bursts of 0.5-2.5 s, their records, the start's ~2 s and the zero's 1 s: 40
  '  MININC   per sign 10 windows (41 s: 2 s each down to the 2 ticks/s rung, then a cycle's 360 counts at the rate, to
  '           10 s at 0.6 ticks/s), a 1 s settle and a ~0.5 s stop each: 56; both signs, with records: 130
  '  LADDER   per sign at 12 V (six rungs): from rest 83 s (each rung's ramp up, 1 s settle, 5 s window, ramp down, rest),
  '           by steps 48 s: 131; both signs, with records: 300 (11.1 V 206, 22.2 V 186)
  '  RAMP     per sign up to 8.6 s, 2 s at the top, down to 6 s, the rest: ~17; both, plus the reversal (two 2V changes
  '           of up to 12 s, three 2 s holds, the stop): 90
  '  STOPS    per sign two top rotations (13-17 s each), two crawl rotations (~6 s), a 15 s and a 3 s time stop, the
  '           rests: ~60; both: 140
  '  COAST    per sign and speed (24 V's 100 %, the worst): up 6 s, settle 1 s, the 2 s steady window, the coast under 1 s,
  '           the 0.3 s quiet, the recovery and the rest ~1 s: ~11; six, with records: 70
  '  OFFSCAN  per sign and speed two sides, each up (to 6 s), seven points of 6 s, down (to 4.5 s), the rest: ~53 at the
  '           top, ~47 at 25 %; 3 speeds x 2 signs x 2 sides, with records: 660 (11 minutes)
  '  PASSPRB  per sign up to 50 % (~3.5 s), settle 1 s, the 10 s window, down ~2.5 s, the rest: ~18; both: 45
  '  COAST and OFFSCAN drive only at a DAT rowL13 row; the estimates (and so the caps) count them at every row.
  '  PHASE 2c, the attended legs, counted as the time their steps RUN (the run's time cap does not count a screen
  '  waiting on him, runIdleMs), each step at its own bounds, three runs of each (a step and two redos):
  '  HANDLOAD per step: the limit and spin-up ~1 s, the grip within HAND_GRIP_WAIT_MS 30 s, the stand ~1.2 s, the stop
  '           and rest ~1 s: ~33; three steps x three runs: 300
  '  HELDPUSH per step: the arm ~0.3 s, a slow turn ~10 s, the release 1 s: ~12; at its bound HELD_WAIT_MS 60 s; two
  '           steps x three runs at a minute: 360
  '  SAG      up to the 22.2 V top ~7.5 s, the settle, the dial-down ~15 s (its bound 120), the stop ~5 s: ~30; three
  '           runs, one at the bound: 180
  '  PINCH    up ~6.4 s, the settle and the 2 s reference, the pinch and DONE ~10 s, the stop ~4.5 s: ~25; three: 75
  '  TASK 3686, the D2 qualification's own legs:
  '  WIRING   checkWiring()'s two legs ~1.3 s (at most 2 x WALK_LEG_TIMEOUT_MS, 4 s), the settle 0.3 s, the records: 10
  '  POWER    per rung from rest: up (to 8.6 s at 11.1 V's top, 5.4 at 12 V's), 1 s settle, the 5 s window, down (to
  '           6 s), the rest: 10-21; per sign four rungs ~70 at 11.1 V; both, with records: 150
    LEG_WIRING_EST_S   = 10
    LEG_POWER_EST_S    = 150
    LEG_HALLMAP_EST_S  = 40
    LEG_MININC_EST_S   = 130
    LEG_LADDER_EST_S   = 300
    LEG_RAMP_EST_S     = 90
    LEG_STOPS_EST_S    = 140
    LEG_COAST_EST_S    = 70
    LEG_OFFSCAN_EST_S  = 660
    LEG_PASSPRB_EST_S  = 45
    LEG_HANDLOAD_EST_S = 300
    LEG_HELDPUSH_EST_S = 360
    LEG_SAG_EST_S      = 180
    LEG_PINCH_EST_S    = 75
    LEGS_2A_EST_S      = (-PART_MININC_BUILT) * LEG_MININC_EST_S + (-PART_LADDER_BUILT) * LEG_LADDER_EST_S + (-PART_RAMP_BUILT) * LEG_RAMP_EST_S + (-PART_STOPS_BUILT) * LEG_STOPS_EST_S
    LEGS_2B_EST_S      = (-PART_COAST_BUILT) * LEG_COAST_EST_S + (-PART_OFFSCAN_BUILT) * LEG_OFFSCAN_EST_S + (-PART_PASSPRB_BUILT) * LEG_PASSPRB_EST_S
    LEGS_2C_EST_S      = (-PART_HANDLOAD_BUILT) * LEG_HANDLOAD_EST_S + (-PART_HELDPUSH_BUILT) * LEG_HELDPUSH_EST_S + (-PART_SAG_BUILT) * LEG_SAG_EST_S + (-PART_PINCH_BUILT) * LEG_PINCH_EST_S
    LEGS_Q_EST_S       = (-PART_WIRING_BUILT) * LEG_WIRING_EST_S + (-PART_POWER_BUILT) * LEG_POWER_EST_S
    LEGS_DRIVEN_EST_S  = LEGS_2A_EST_S + LEGS_2B_EST_S + LEGS_2C_EST_S + LEGS_Q_EST_S   ' every leg after the hall map's crawl
    LEGS_EST_S         = (-PART_HALLMAP_BUILT) * LEG_HALLMAP_EST_S + LEGS_DRIVEN_EST_S

  ' RUN_TIME_CAP_S: the longest a run may take, RUN_TIME_FACTOR x the legs built (DERIVED). Phase 1 capped the hall map
  '  alone at 5 x 40 = 200 s; a chained run was ~700 s at phase 2a, and 5 x that is an hour of an unwatched motor, so 3 x:
  '  the hall map alone 120 s, the 2a chain 2_100 s. Phase 2b: every leg is 1_475 s (25 minutes at a rowL13 row, 13 where
  '  COAST and OFFSCAN skip), so the chain's cap is 4_425 s (74 minutes); each leg's own bounds end a stuck drive long
  '  before it. Phase 2c: an attended tier builds its one leg, so its cap is 3 x that leg's running time (900 s for
  '  HANDLOAD, 1_080 HELDPUSH, 540 SAG, 225 PINCH), and the time spent on a screen waiting for him is not counted.
  '  Task 3686: the qualification chain (WIRING, POWER, LADDER, RAMP, STOPS) is 690 s, so its cap is 2_070 s.
    RUN_TIME_FACTOR    = 3
    RUN_TIME_CAP_S     = RUN_TIME_FACTOR * LEGS_EST_S

  ' RUN_CHARGE_CAP_MAS: the run's DC-link charge cap, mA x s -- the phase 1 base (a minute at the rated current) plus the
  '  sheet's no-load ceiling over every driven leg built (CON { the Doco's numbers }, RUN_CHARGE_BASE_MAS's note). Every
  '  hands-off leg: 110_400 + 400 x 1_435 = 684_400 (0.19 Ah). An attended tier: 110_400 + 400 x its leg (HANDLOAD
  '  230_400, HELDPUSH 254_400, SAG 182_400, PINCH 140_400); HANDLOAD's stalls are bounded first by its own two caps.
  '  Task 3686, the qualification chain: 110_400 + 400 x 690 = 386_400.
    RUN_CHARGE_CAP_MAS = RUN_CHARGE_BASE_MAS + NO_LOAD_MA_MAX * LEGS_DRIVEN_EST_S

CON { run sequencing enums }

  ' The four sets of the hall map, one per increment sign and crawl rung:
  '  SET_NEG_SLOW - negative increments at HALLMAP_SLOW_TPS
  '  SET_POS_SLOW - positive increments at HALLMAP_SLOW_TPS
  '  SET_NEG_FAST - negative increments at HALLMAP_FAST_TPS
  '  SET_POS_FAST - positive increments at HALLMAP_FAST_TPS
    #0, SET_NEG_SLOW, SET_POS_SLOW, SET_NEG_FAST, SET_POS_FAST
    SET_COUNT  = SET_POS_FAST + 1
    SET_CELLS  = SET_COUNT * HALL_TICKS_PER_REV             ' one accumulator per set per sector slot

  ' A set is its rung and its sign: SET_* = rung x SIGN_COUNT + sign, so the slow rung's two sets come first.
  '  RUNG_SLOW / RUNG_FAST - HALLMAP_SLOW_TPS / HALLMAP_FAST_TPS
  '  SIGN_NEG / SIGN_POS   - negative / positive increments
    #0, RUNG_SLOW, RUNG_FAST
    #0, SIGN_NEG, SIGN_POS
    SIGN_COUNT = SIGN_POS + 1

  ' A burst's outcome:
  '  BO_RUNNING      - still driving (never leaves bRunBurst())
  '  BO_DONE         - every edge it needed, stopped and settled
  '  BO_FAULT        - the driver faulted
  '  BO_OVER_CURRENT - the DC link stayed over ABS_ABORT_MA for ABS_ABORT_SAMPLES samples
  '  BO_CHARGE_CAP   - the run's charge reached RUN_CHARGE_CAP_MAS
  '  BO_STALL        - no hall edge for HALLMAP_STALL_MS while driven
  '  BO_TIMEOUT      - the burst outlasted its bound
  '  BO_TIME_CAP     - the run reached RUN_TIME_CAP_S
  '  BO_REFUSED      - the library refused the drive or its stop
  '  BO_STEP_CAP     - phase 2c: a hand-load step's stall charge reached HAND_STEP_CAP_MAS (that step's motor is
  '                    stopped; the run goes on)
  '  BO_LEG_CAP      - phase 2c: the hand-load leg's stall charge reached HAND_LEG_CAP_MAS (the run ends)
    #0, BO_RUNNING, BO_DONE, BO_FAULT, BO_OVER_CURRENT, BO_CHARGE_CAP, BO_STALL, BO_TIMEOUT, BO_TIME_CAP, BO_REFUSED, ...
        BO_STEP_CAP, BO_LEG_CAP
    BO_TOKENS = BO_LEG_CAP + 1

  ' Why the run ended early (the first cause is kept, never overwritten):
  '  AR_NONE      - it did not
  '  AR_NOT_DOCO  - not built for the Doco bench (-D BENCH_CFG -D BENCH_DOCO): nothing was started
  '  AR_NO_PART   - no leg compiled in (no -D SINGLE_PART_*): nothing was started
  '  AR_BOARD     - the board read is not EXPECTED_BOARD (detail: the REV_* read); nothing was driven
  '  AR_START     - start() refused (detail: its ERR_*)
  '  AR_LIMITS    - the test current limit was not taken (detail: its ERR_*, or the peak read back)
  '  AR_ENC_START - the encoder did not start (detail: its ENC_ERR_*)
  '  AR_ZERO      - the current sense's rest zero is not healthy (detail: its mean, mV x10): no current guard could work
  '  AR_BURST     - a burst did not complete (detail: its BO_*)
  '  AR_ENC_CHECK - the encoder self-check failed (detail: its CHK_*, named in the record)
  '  AR_ROW       - the told voltage has no row in DAT rowMv (detail: TOLD_MV); nothing was driven
  '  AR_GUARD     - a 2a leg's guard ended the run (detail: its BO_*: OVER_CURRENT, CHARGE_CAP or TIME_CAP)
  '  AR_ENC_WIN   - a 2a window's encoder disagreed with the driver's hall position (detail: |dev| counts, or -1 the sign)
  '  AR_CAP       - the library wrote an increment past the row's top for a power command (detail: that increment)
  '  AR_SETTING   - a 2b leg's setting was not taken, or not restored on its exit (detail: the library's error, or -1
  '                 when it read back otherwise): the fault response (L-coast) or the commutation offsets (L-offscan);
  '                 phase 2c: the hold limits or the hold mode (L-heldpush)
  '  AR_WORKER    - phase 2c: the measure cog did not start (detail: cogspin()'s result); nothing was driven
  '  AR_WIRING    - task 3686: L-wiring's walk did not pass (detail: getHealth()'s failed HLT_* bits, or checkWiring()'s
  '                 error): a motor whose wiring is not proven is driven no further
    #0, AR_NONE, AR_NOT_DOCO, AR_NO_PART, AR_BOARD, AR_START, AR_LIMITS, AR_ENC_START, AR_ZERO, AR_BURST, AR_ENC_CHECK, ...
        AR_ROW, AR_GUARD, AR_ENC_WIN, AR_CAP, AR_SETTING, AR_WORKER, AR_WIRING
    AR_TOKENS = AR_WIRING + 1

  ' How a 2a leg's measured drive ended (RO_ = run outcome):
  '  RO_NOT_RUN  - not reached (the run ended first)
  '  RO_DONE     - driven, measured, ended as planned
  '  RO_FAULT    - the driver faulted (or re-synced) on it: a finding; cleared with testResetFault()
  '  RO_REFUSED  - the library refused the command (a latched protective stop is cleared after it)
  '  RO_SKIPPED  - not driven: an earlier rung of the same entry faulted (the ladder), or was not steady (L-mininc)
  '  RO_TIMEOUT  - it did not arrive (or come to rest) within its bound: measured anyway, then stopped
  '  RO_ABORTED  - a guard ended the run during it
  '  RO_WALL     - L-offscan: the point met the current wall (the scan's point abort); its side ends there
  '  RO_STOPPED  - phase 2c: the operator clicked STOP MOTOR (L-pinch)
    #0, RO_NOT_RUN, RO_DONE, RO_FAULT, RO_REFUSED, RO_SKIPPED, RO_TIMEOUT, RO_ABORTED, RO_WALL, RO_STOPPED
    RO_TOKENS = RO_STOPPED + 1

  ' L-offscan's two sides of the shipped offset: SIDE_PLUS steps it up, SIDE_MINUS down (each from the shipped one)
    #0, SIDE_PLUS, SIDE_MINUS
    OFS_SPEED_SLOTS = SIGN_COUNT * SPEED_PCT_COUNT          ' one fit per sign and speed
  ' L-offscan's two fitted quantities: FITQ_DC the DC link (the current minimum), FITQ_DUTY the duty
    #0, FITQ_DC, FITQ_DUTY
    FITQ_COUNT = FITQ_DUTY + 1

  ' Phase 2c. L-handload's steps by their limit, in DAT handLimitA's order: HL_4A, HL_2A, HL_DEF (the default limits).
  '  The panel's step ids are these plus SG_STEP_HL_4A (the generated table keeps the same order)
    #0, HL_4A, HL_2A, HL_DEF
    HL_COUNT = HL_DEF + 1
  ' How a hand-load step ended (HE_ = hand end):
  '  HE_NONE      - not run
  '  HE_LATCHED   - the blocked stop latched (the event under test)
  '  HE_NO_LATCH  - the shaft stood HAND_NOLATCH_MS with no hall tick and no latch: the program stopped the drive
  '  HE_STEP_CAP  - the step's stall charge reached HAND_STEP_CAP_MAS first: the program stopped the drive
  '  HE_STOPPED   - he clicked STOP MOTOR
  '  HE_NO_GRIP   - no grip within HAND_GRIP_WAIT_MS of arriving
  '  HE_TIMEOUT   - the ACT reached HAND_ACT_MAX_MS (a grip that never stood)
  '  HE_FAULT     - the driver faulted (or re-synced) under the hand: a finding
  '  HE_NO_SPEED  - it never reached AT_SPEED in its bound
  '  HE_REFUSED   - the library refused the drive
  '  HE_ABORTED   - a guard ended the run during it
  '  HE_SETUP     - the step's limit did not take
    #0, HE_NONE, HE_LATCHED, HE_NO_LATCH, HE_STEP_CAP, HE_STOPPED, HE_NO_GRIP, HE_TIMEOUT, HE_FAULT, HE_NO_SPEED, ...
        HE_REFUSED, HE_ABORTED, HE_SETUP
    HE_TOKENS = HE_SETUP + 1
  ' L-heldpush's two measured directions (the halls' order, never "forward"): DIR_RISE, DIR_FALL
    #0, DIR_RISE, DIR_FALL
    DIR_COUNT = DIR_FALL + 1
  ' How a sag step ended (SO_ = sag outcome):
  '  SO_NONE        - not run
  '  SO_FAULT_FIRST - a fault (or a re-sync) before the speed fell SAG_LOST_PM under its command
  '  SO_SLIP_FIRST  - the speed fell under SAG_LOST_PM of its command for SAG_LOST_MS with no fault yet
  '  SO_STOPPED     - he clicked STOP MOTOR before either
  '  SO_NO_LOSS     - neither within SAG_WAIT_MS
  '  SO_NO_SPEED    - it never reached AT_SPEED (or its settle faulted) in its bound
  '  SO_REFUSED     - the library refused the drive
  '  SO_ABORTED     - a guard ended the run during it
    #0, SO_NONE, SO_FAULT_FIRST, SO_SLIP_FIRST, SO_STOPPED, SO_NO_LOSS, SO_NO_SPEED, SO_REFUSED, SO_ABORTED
    SO_TOKENS = SO_ABORTED + 1

  ' The ladder's two entries to a rung: ENTRY_REST from rest on the built-in ramp, ENTRY_STEP from the rung below
    #0, ENTRY_REST, ENTRY_STEP
    ENTRY_COUNT = ENTRY_STEP + 1
    LADDER_SLOTS = SIGN_COUNT * ENTRY_COUNT * LADDER_MAX_RUNGS

  ' The stop legs' two speeds: KIND_TOP (the row's top power) and KIND_CRAWL (STOPS_CRAWL_POWER)
    #0, KIND_TOP, KIND_CRAWL
    KIND_COUNT = KIND_CRAWL + 1
  ' The ramp leg's two changes: CHG_UP (from rest to the top) and CHG_DN (stopMotor() from the top)
    #0, CHG_UP, CHG_DN
    CHG_COUNT = CHG_DN + 1
  ' R23-SGL-SMOOTH's three instances: the NEG and POS ceilings (SIGN_*), and the reversal
    SMOOTH_REVERSAL = SIGN_COUNT
    SMOOTH_COUNT    = SMOOTH_REVERSAL + 1
    MININC_SLOTS    = SIGN_COUNT * MININC_RUNGS
    STOPS_SLOTS     = SIGN_COUNT * KIND_COUNT * (STOPS_ROT_COUNT + 1)    ' per sign and kind: the rotations, then the time

  ' The hall code order the position RISES through (TECHNIQUES.md 1.2): codes 1-5-4-6-2-3. MIRRORED on purpose, as
  '  test_bench_dual's LIB_* constants are: the instrument classifies each edge by its own table, not the driver's.
    HALL_ORDER_LEN   = 6
    NOT_IN_ORDER     = -1                                   ' an illegal code (%000 or %111)
    NO_BOUNDARY      = -1                                   ' a slot that has not seen an edge yet
    TICK_RISE        = 1
    TICK_FALL        = -1
    TICK_BAD         = 0                                    ' a skipped or illegal transition: no boundary, no tick
    CODE_PREV_SHIFT  = 4                                    ' edgeCodes[]: new code in bits 0..2, the previous in 4..6
    CODE_MASK        = %111

CON { sampling and windows }

    SAMPLE_MS           = 5                                 ' the guard and telemetry cadence while driven (the scan's)
    ZERO_SAMPLES        = 200                               ' the rest-zero reading, ~1 s (the scan's)
    ZERO_SPREAD_MIN_MV  = 1                                 ' a live channel's readings differ (min <> max), the scan's R12 rule
    READY_TIMEOUT_MS    = 2_000                             ' the driver reports ready after start()
    READY_POLL_MS       = 2
    STOP_SETTLE_MS      = 300                               ' after the drive reports stopped: the last edges still arrive
    BURST_MARGIN_MS     = 2_000                             ' a burst's bound: twice its edges' time at the rung, plus this
    BURST_TIME_FACTOR   = 2
    X10                 = 10                                ' the scale of every _x10 field
    UA_PER_MA           = 1_000                             ' mV x 1_000 / (mV per A) is mA
    PM                  = 1_000                             ' per mille: the whole of every _pm field
    X100                = 100
    US_PER_S            = 1_000_000

  ' PHASE 2a: the sampler (sampleNext()) and the measuring windows -- harness mechanics, carried unchanged to any motor
    ARR_RING            = 8                                 ' the arrival speed: the last 8 readings, 35 ms (it lags 18 ms)
    REST_RING           = 128                               ' the rest instant: the last 128 readings, 635 ms
    LADDER_SETTLE_MS    = 1_000                             ' at a rung after arriving, before its window
    LADDER_WINDOW_MS    = 5_000                             ' the measuring window: with the settle, each rung is held >= 5 s
    LEG_REST_MS         = 500                               ' at rest between drives (the bridge coasts; the halls settle)
    ARRIVE_MARGIN_MS    = 2_000                             ' a change's bound: twice the generator's time, plus this
    REST_WAIT_MAX_MS    = 3_000                             ' the rest wait's bound once the drive reports the move done
    MININC_SETTLE_MS    = 1_000                             ' a crawl rung from rest: the ramp takes < 0.4 s at 24 ticks/s
    MININC_MIN_WIN_MS   = 2_000                             ' the shortest window ...
    MININC_MAX_WIN_MS   = 10_000                            ' ... and the longest (a cycle at 0.6 ticks/s): past a signed getct()
                                                            '  difference at 350 MHz (6.1 s), so a crawl window is timed by getms()
    RAMP_HOLD_MS        = 2_000                             ' L-ramp: at the top after arriving, before the stop
    REV_HOLD_MS         = 2_000                             ' L-ramp's reversal: at each top
    STOPS_DRIVE_MAX_MS  = 40_000                            ' L-stops: a limited drive's bound (the longest, 400 rev at 7.4 V, ~17 s)
    WINCHK_TOL_COUNTS   = 2 * ENC_COUNTS_PER_TICK + enc.CHECK_TOL_COUNTS    ' 122: a window's two ends each read a whole tick
    ARRIVE_BAND_PM      = 30                                ' L-ramp: "arrived" is within 3 % of the change's end (FOLLOW's band)

  ' PHASE 2c: the panel and the measure cog -- harness mechanics, carried unchanged from T0-24 (test_bench_t0.spin2
  '  T0_24_UI_*, T0_24_JOB_POLL_US, T0_24_WORKER_STACK), the panel that ran on this rig (PL-127)
    SG_UI_WAIT_MS       = 10                                ' the panel loop's wait: one PC_MOUSE read every pass
    SG_UI_DEBOUNCE_MS   = 300                               ' after a screen change a press is ignored this long (logged IGNORED)
    SG_UI_REDRAW_MS     = 200                               ' live readings redraw at most five times a second
    SG_FINAL_WAIT_MS    = 120_000                           ' the last screen waits this long for FINISH, then the session ends
    SG_MOUSE_LONGS      = 7                                 ' PC_MOUSE: xpos, ypos, wheeldelta, lbutton, mbutton, rbutton, pixel
    SG_MOUSE_XPOS       = 0
    SG_MOUSE_YPOS       = 1
    SG_MOUSE_LBTN       = 3
    SG_INPUT_MAX        = 16                                ' presses kept per screen for B1-UI (more are counted, not kept)
    SG_INPUT_LONGS      = 4                                 ' a kept press: x, y, the button it hit (or SG_HIT_*), ms into the screen
    SG_HIT_MISS         = -1                                ' a press that landed on no live button
    SG_HIT_IGNORED      = -2                                ' a press inside the debounce after a screen change
    WK_JOB_POLL_US      = 200                               ' the idle measure cog's wait between looks at the mailbox
    WK_STACK_LONGS      = 600                               ' the measure cog's stack: T0-24's, the deepest job being a step's loop
    WK_EV_READ_MAX      = 40                                ' bound on one read of the event log (T0_24_EV_READ_MAX)
    HAND_STAND_SHOW_MS  = 50                                ' L-handload's panel says STANDING once no tick has come this long
    HAND_RING_MA_N      = 10                                ' the live current reading: the last 10 readings' mean, 50 ms

CON { cells -- sign-off format sf 1 (DOCs/plans/VISIT-SIGNOFF-DESIGN.md sec B.1) }

    SF_VERSION = 1

    ' R23-SGL-ENCCHK, crit ENC_DEV, units COUNTS, one instance per set: the worst |enc - 60 x ticks| over the set's bursts,
    '  each burst's span from its first captured edge to the edge BURST_SPAN_TICKS later (exactly two revolutions).
    ' PRECONDITION: a burst that captured BURST_SPAN_EDGES edges; its encoder counts and its hall ticks are taken at the same
    '  captured edges, so they are one observation (never two reads apart). The drive cannot erase it: the halls and the
    '  encoder are read, never commanded. A set with no such burst is NOMEAS.
    ' BOUND: 0 .. enc.CHECK_TOL_COUNTS (2): the encoder object's own derivation (its capture under 0.03 count, one count of
    '  rounding at each end). Phase 2a: both ends are the PASM capture's own latched counts (takeEdge()), so nothing is
    '  added (phase 1's polled capture, ENC_POLL_SKEW_X100 17, is retired with it).
    ' CORRECT CASE: 48 ticks over two revolutions read 2,880 counts, dev 0 (0..2 with rounding) -> PASS. Broken: B not
    '  counted reads ~1,440, dev 1,440; A and B swapped reads -2,880 against +48 ticks, dev 5,760; one transition skipped
    '  inside the span reads 47 ticks against 2,880 counts, dev 60; all FAIL, and the run stops with the CHK_* name.
    '  No unfixed code exists: the instrument is new; these negatives are the desk mutations (python model, task 3679).
    '  Rival: a slipping coupling also reads TOO-FEW; a lost B line reads HALF-RATE, which the encoder object names apart.
    ENCCHK_LO_COUNTS = 0

    ' R23-SGL-SECTOR, crit SECTOR_DEV_X10, units CNT_X10 (tenths of a count: tenths of an ELECTRICAL degree on this motor),
    '  one instance per set: the worst |width - 60 counts| of the 24 hall sectors of a revolution. A width is the difference
    '  of two adjacent boundary positions, each the mean of that boundary's edges over the set's SECTOR_REVS revolutions.
    ' PRECONDITION: the set completed SECTOR_REVS revolutions in encoder-checked bursts; otherwise NOMEAS. That excludes a
    '  set with a LOST edge, which is ENCCHK's negative; this cell's own negatives (a displaced sensor, a glitching sensor,
    '  a sensor more than half a sector off) leave a whole-revolution span exact, so the exclusion cannot hide them. A
    '  slot holding other than one edge per revolution, a slot that saw two boundaries, or two adjacent slots whose
    '  boundaries do not step by one, is NOT excluded: the set reads SECTOR_BROKEN_X10 and FAILs. The drive cannot move a
    '  hall boundary.
    ' BOUND: 0 .. SECTOR_TOL_X10 (60: 6 counts = 6 electrical degrees = 1.5 mechanical). DERIVED, PROVISIONAL (arbiter):
    '  the driver places the field from the hall sector and one offset for all six (BLDC-COMMUTATION-PRINCIPLES.md), so a
    '  boundary off the equal grid by d places that sector's field d off; at 6 degrees torque per amp falls 1 - cos 6 =
    '  0.55 %, inside the 1-3 % residual the misdial check allows (analysis sec 8, L2) and far inside the +-15 degree basin
    '  where the current minimum is flat to a few percent. A width off by w moves at least one of its two boundaries.
    ' CORRECT CASE: equal sectors read 600 x10 per sector, +-10 x10 for the count's own quantum at the two ends (the latched
    '  count is whole, and every crossing of one boundary one way latches the same count, so averaging does not remove it;
    '  the PASM capture adds under 0.1 x10) -> dev 0..10 -> (phase 1 wrote +-0.4 here, leaving the quantum out; 2a corrects it)
    '  PASS. Negative: one sensor 8 counts from its place reads widths 520 and 680 -> dev 80 -> FAIL; a sensor 40 counts off
    '  puts its edges in the neighbouring slot -> SECTOR_BROKEN_X10 -> FAIL.
    '  No unfixed code exists (a first measurement of the motor); the negatives are the desk mutations (python model).
    '  Rival: a timing error that DIFFERS BETWEEN SENSORS (unequal hall IC delays) also makes unequal widths, and grows
    '  with speed where geometry does not: B1-SPDCMP's max_wdiff_x10 (the same sector's width at the two rungs) separates
    '  them -- MODELED, a sensor displaced 8 counts reads 0 there, a sensor lagging 8 counts more at the fast rung reads 80.
    '  A timing error COMMON to the three sensors shifts every edge alike: widths unchanged, the zero moves (z_diff_x10).
    SECTOR_LO_X10     = 0
    SECTOR_TOL_X10    = 60
    SECTOR_BROKEN_X10 = 9_999                               ' a map whose slots are not one boundary each: not a width

    ' ---- PHASE 2a cells. Each names its feeding leg; a declared cell's leg is always built with it (emitSignoffDecls()).
    '  The reference cells (FOLLOW, SMOOTH, RAMPARR, STOPROT, STOPTIME) judge TODAY'S drive on the shipped tables: their
    '  unfixed value is today's, measured first at D1, and a FAIL is a finding. Every negative named below is a desk
    '  mutation of this harness's own arithmetic (the python model sgl2a_model.py, task 3679 phase 2a; 55 of 55 checks
    '  agree), and every correct-case number is that model's.

    ' R23-SGL-MININC (L-mininc), crit MIN_STEADY_TPSX100, units TPS_X100, one instance per increment sign: the smallest rate
    '  of the descending sweep that turned steadily (CON { the Doco's numbers }, STEADY) with every faster rung steady;
    '  MININC_NONE_TPS_X100 when the first did not.
    ' PRECONDITION: the sweep's first rung was driven (to its window's end, or to a fault); each verdict needs its whole
    '  window, timed by getms(); the encoder sees a stall the drive cannot hide. A sign whose first rung never ran: NOMEAS.
    ' BOUND: 0 .. MININC_HI_TPS_X100 (146): the shipped minimum, 544_628 = 1.4555 ticks/s by the drive law, rounded up so
    '  its own rung passes: PASS says the table's floor turns steadily.
    ' CORRECT CASE: a synchronous crawl down to 0.6 ticks/s reads 60 -> PASS; the 2023 note ("anything below yields NO
    '  rotation") predicts 146 (its rung steady, 1 tick/s not) -> PASS at the edge. Broken: a rotor that stalls below 3
    '  ticks/s reads 300; one that slips a pole pair at 2 ticks/s (travel 360 short) reads 300; a first rung that stutters
    '  reads 99_999: all FAIL. UNFIXED: today's drive, measured first at D1 (the forward sign's shipped minimum, 1, is
    '  PL-71's table defect and sec 6's, not this cell's: the cell judges the rate the motor holds).
    '  Rival: cogging the drive's floor torque cannot pull through stalls the rotor by the motor's own physics, not the
    '  drive's: B1-MININC's duty and held separate them -- stalled at the duty floor with no held pass is the floor's torque;
    '  duty risen and passes held is the lag limiter.
    MININC_LO_TPS_X100   = 0
    MININC_HI_TPS_X100   = 146
    MININC_NONE_TPS_X100 = 99_999

    ' R23-SGL-FOLLOW (L-ladder), crit FOL_DEV_PM, units PERMILLE, one instance per increment sign: the worst |encoder speed
    '  / commanded - 1| over the ladder's table rungs (25-100 % of the ceiling), from rest and by a step; a rung that
    '  faulted reads PM (it did not hold its speed).
    ' PRECONDITION: the rung's window ran (5 s, after arriving and a 1 s settle) or the rung faulted; a skipped rung follows
    '  a fault already counted. Each speed is the encoder's travel over the window's own getct() span, never two reads apart.
    ' BOUND: 0 .. FOLLOW_TOL_PM (30): plan sec 7, "encoder speed within 3 % of command" (the 6.5in's SPINRATE_FOL_LO 97).
    ' CORRECT CASE: P-S1 (MODELED): every rung of the 7.4-24 V rows at 100.0 % -> dev 0..1 (a count in >= 70_000) -> PASS.
    '  At 11.1 V the model faults the top (P-S2) -> PM -> FAIL, a finding. Broken: a field slipping to 96.0 % reads 41 ->
    '  FAIL. UNFIXED: today's drive; 2023's notes put each row's top on its speed, as the model does but at 11.1 V.
    '  Rival: an encoder coupling that slips reads slow too; the window's encoder check against the driver's hall position
    '  (bWindowEncOk()) separates them -- a slipping coupling disagrees with the halls and ends the run, a rotor behind its
    '  field agrees with them.
    FOLLOW_LO_PM  = 0
    FOLLOW_TOL_PM = 30

    ' R23-SGL-MISDIAL (L-ladder), crit VPRED_DEV_PM, units PERMILLE, one instance per increment sign: (the supply the duty
    '  line predicts - TOLD_MV) / TOLD_MV. The line is least squares of duty against the encoder's speed over the clean rungs
    '  (arrived, no fault, no held, capped or folded pass, following within FOLLOW_TOL_PM).
    ' PRECONDITION: MISDIAL_MIN_POINTS clean rungs spanning MISDIAL_MIN_SPAN_PM of the fastest one's speed, the line rising;
    '  otherwise NOMEAS. A FAIL marks every B1-RUNG of this run usable FALSE (both signs: the supply is one).
    ' BOUND: -MISDIAL_TOL_PM .. +MISDIAL_TOL_PM: 130 while KE_IS_FITTED is FALSE (all of D1, in the run), 30 once a build
    '  sets it TRUE (D2); D1's evaluation applies the 30 offline to the logged ratio_ppm (arbiter decision D5, CON { the
    '  Doco's numbers }, THE MISDIAL CHECK).
    ' CORRECT CASE: the model's 12 V ladder (P-S3, duty 20-71 % over 560-2,238 rpm) predicts 11.94 V -> -5 -> PASS; its 24 V
    '  ladder 23.69 V -> -13 -> PASS. Broken: told 12 V with 24 V set halves every duty -> +990 -> FAIL; told 24 V with 22.2 V
    '  set -> -87: PASS unfitted (not resolved), FAIL once fitted. UNFIXED: nothing checks a told voltage today.
    '  Rival: a Ke off the sheet (or the duty-to-volts scale off) moves every row's prediction by one factor, a misdial one
    '  row's: across D1's rows a common ratio is the motor (fit it; KE_IS_FITTED), a lone row is that row's supply.
    '  TASK 3686, the D2 build (SINGLE_QUALIFY): fitted, +-30, predicting from KE_FITTED_MV_PER_KRPM. Desk model
    '  (sgl3686_model.py): 12 V -5 and 24 V -13 PASS; told 24 V set 22.2 V -87, told 12 V set 11.1 V -80, FAIL; a motor
    '  whose Ke is 5 % under the sheet reads +47 and FAILS on the sheet's value, -5 on its fitted one -- the fitted Ke is
    '  a D2 precondition. THE EXCLUSION CHECK: a clean rung excludes a capped, held or folded one; the fitted negative (an
    '  adjacent row) raises the top duty to 45-77 % of duty_max, under the 92.5 % reserve, so no rung it needs is
    '  excluded. A supply far under the told one caps the top rungs and can leave fewer than MISDIAL_MIN_POINTS clean:
    '  NOMEAS here, and FOLLOW, POWER and TOPSPD are the cells that fail it (a capped rotor falls behind its field, which
    '  the lag hold then holds back, or it faults: SMOOTH).
    MISDIAL_FIT_TOL_PM = 30
    MISDIAL_TOL_PM     = MISDIAL_FIT_TOL_PM + (KE_IS_FITTED + 1) * KE_SHEET_TOL_PCT * X10   ' 130, or 30 once fitted (TRUE is -1)

    ' R23-SGL-SMOOTH (L-ladder, L-ramp), crit FAULT_RUNS, units COUNT, instances NEG and POS -- the ceiling: the ladder's
    '  100 % rung from rest and by a step, and L-ramp's top run -- and REVERSAL (L-ramp's top to the other top and back):
    '  the runs that faulted or re-synced.
    ' PRECONDITION: the run was commanded and driven to its end or to its fault; an instance no built leg feeds is neither
    '  declared nor printed.
    ' BOUND: 0 .. 0: plan sec 7, "the ceiling runs smoothly: no lag fault, no re-sync ... forward, reverse and reversals".
    ' CORRECT CASE: P-S1 / P-S4 (MODELED, Lh <= 1 mH): every top clean -> 0 -> PASS; 11.1 V's climb faults (P-S2) -> 1 or
    '  more -> FAIL, a finding. Broken: one re-sync on a step entry -> 1 -> FAIL. UNFIXED: today's drive; the 2023 note
    '  "reverse still not working reliably" (1f4b4d0) is the reversal's only prior.
    '  Rival: a supply that sags at the climb (a bench supply's current limit) faults a top without the drive being at
    '  fault: the same run's misdial check and the climb's DC link (B1-RAMP up_dc_ma) say whether the supply held.
    SMOOTH_LO = 0
    SMOOTH_HI = 0

    ' R23-SGL-RAMPARR (L-ramp), crit ARR_DEV_PM, units PERMILLE, instances NEG-UP, NEG-DN, POS-UP, POS-DN: (the encoder's
    '  arrival - the generator's prediction) / the prediction. UP: from the command at rest to the encoder within
    '  ARRIVE_BAND_PM of the top's speed; DN: from stopMotor() to under ARRIVE_BAND_PM of the speed it stopped from.
    ' PRECONDITION: the drive left rest (UP) / held the top (DN), no fault; the prediction is the S-curve (scurveMs()) from
    '  the drive's own limits (testGetRampLimits()) and the increment the library wrote, to the same band as the reading.
    '  TASK 3686 (the exclusion check): an arrival the encoder never reads before the change's bound (twice the
    '  generator's whole time plus ARRIVE_MARGIN_MS: the climb, or the stop, ran to it) READS THAT BOUND, at least +1_000
    '  -- a FAIL, never a NOMEAS. Before, it was not judged: the slowest ramps, this cell's own negative, were the ones
    '  excluded (sgl3686_model.py: 0.3 x the limits read NOMEAS; now +1_499 -> FAIL). DN no longer needs DCS_STOPPED.
    ' BOUND: -RAMPARR_TOL_PM .. +RAMPARR_TOL_PM (100): RAMPARR's bar (the 6.5in's RAMPARR_PCT 10).
    ' CORRECT CASE: at the 12 V top (335e6) 5_127 ms predicted to 97 %; the 35 ms speed reading lags 18 ms -> +4 -> PASS.
    '  Broken: a generator at half the built-in acceleration -> +979 -> FAIL; at 0.88 of it -> +137 -> FAIL. UNFIXED: the 6.5in's
    '  RAMPARR read two legs of four 59 % and 118 % late (the path limiter); the Doco unloaded is predicted on time (P-R1).
    '  Rival: a rotor held back by a current limit (fold-back) arrives late with the generator on time: B1-RAMP's
    '  at_state_ms (the drive's own AT_SPEED), folds and held separate them.
    RAMPARR_TOL_PM = 100

    ' R23-SGL-STOPROT (L-stops), crit REST_DEV_COUNTS, units COUNTS, instances NEG-TOP, NEG-CRWL, POS-TOP, POS-CRWL: the
    '  encoder's travel from the arming to rest less N x 60, signed; of the kind's two N, the larger in size.
    ' PRECONDITION: armed at rest (its base exact: nothing moves), the drive ended SR_AT_LIMIT, the shaft read at rest
    '  (REST_QUIET_MS); a drive that ended otherwise is not judged (its record says why) -- EXCEPT, task 3686 (the
    '  exclusion check), a limit that never fired in STOPS_DRIVE_MAX_MS: before, it was not judged, so this cell's own
    '  negative read NOMEAS; now it is judged at the stop the harness then makes (bStopAndRest()), its travel to that
    '  rest (sgl3686_model.py: 300 revolutions at the 12 V top read +1_672_419, the crawl's 120 ticks +216_806 -> FAIL).
    ' BOUND: -STOPROT_EARLY_COUNTS (240) .. +STOPROT_LATE_COUNTS (180): the 6.5in's ROTSTOP band in ticks (test_bench_t0
    '  T0_25_ROT_TOL_TICKS 3 = the doc's "within about two hall ticks" + a whole tick late; T0_25_PLAN_EARLY_TICKS 1 more
    '  early), 60 counts a tick.
    ' CORRECT CASE: at a crawl the stop lands within a tick -> |dev| <= 60 -> PASS. At the tops P-T1 (DERIVED) puts the
    '  field up to +1.05 ticks late (24 V; +1.46 at 11.1 V) from the 1 ms front pass alone, the rotor up to 1.1 tick behind
    '  it: inside the band, near its late edge at 11.1 V. Broken: a planner that ignores the stopping distance overshoots by
    '  it (70 revolutions at the 12 V top) -> FAIL. UNFIXED: the 6.5in's ROTSTOP passed at ~59 ticks/s; the Doco's tops run
    '  15-25 x that hall rate and are the untested case.
    '  Rival: a coupling slipping in the stop changes the travel the encoder reads: B1-STOPROT's pos_ticks (the driver's own
    '  hall travel) beside it separates them.
    STOPROT_EARLY_COUNTS = 4 * ENC_COUNTS_PER_TICK
    STOPROT_LATE_COUNTS  = 3 * ENC_COUNTS_PER_TICK

    ' R23-SGL-STOPTIME (L-stops), crit REST_DEV_MS, units MS, instances as STOPROT's: the shaft's rest instant less the
    '  deadline the library armed (testGetStopMs()), signed; of the kind's one drive.
    ' PRECONDITION: armed at rest, SR_AT_LIMIT, the shaft read at rest; otherwise not judged -- except, task 3686 (as
    '  STOPROT's), a limit that never fired in STOPS_DRIVE_MAX_MS, judged at the harness's own stop: its DCS_STOPPED
    '  reading less the deadline (sgl3686_model.py: +28_758 at the 12 V top -> FAIL; before, NOMEAS).
    ' BOUND: -STOPTIME_TOL_MS .. +STOPTIME_TOL_MS (100): the doc's "at rest by the limit (within a few milliseconds)" at the
    '  shaft's own resolution -- the S-curve's last count takes 46 ms (CON { the Doco's numbers }, THE REST) -- twice that.
    ' CORRECT CASE: a field at zero on the deadline leaves the shaft's last count 0-55 ms before it -> -55..0 -> PASS. Broken:
    '  a planner that starts the stop at the deadline rests one stop late (3_711 ms at the 12 V top) -> FAIL; 150 ms late
    '  reads 101 -> FAIL. UNFIXED: the
    '  6.5in's field-zero band, -6 .. +4 ms (test_bench_t0 T0_25_TIME_*); the field's own zero prints beside (field_dev_ms).
    '  Rival: a shaft coasting on after its field stopped (no hold: holdAtStop(FALSE)) reads late with the planner on time:
    '  field_dev_ms (the drive's own zero instant) separates them.
    STOPTIME_TOL_MS = 100

    ' ---- PHASE 2b cells. Every negative named below is a desk mutation of this harness's own arithmetic or a stated
    '  physical case, run in the python model sgl2b_model.py (task 3679 phase 2b); every correct-case number is DERIVED
    '  or that model's.

    ' R23-SGL-COAST (L-coast), crit COAST_MS, units MS, one instance per increment sign: the time from the first reading of
    '  DCS_FAULTED after the forced fault to the shaft's rest (the first reading of the final REST_QUIET_MS run within
    '  REST_JITTER_COUNTS), from the row's 100 % speed; a shaft still turning at COAST_WAIT_MAX_MS reads COAST_WAIT_MAX_MS
    '  (at least that long: past every bound, so a FAIL, never a NOMEAS). The 25 and 50 % coasts are records only (they
    '  feed the fit).
    ' PRECONDITION: the steady window ran at the speed (arrived, encoder-checked, following within FOLLOW_TOL_PM: the bound
    '  is for that speed); the fault read DCS_FAULTED within COAST_FAULT_WAIT_MS; the state stayed DCS_FAULTED to the end
    '  of the reading (nothing drove or re-synced the bridge); testResetFault() then cleared it; the hold was off.
    '  Otherwise NOMEAS, and B1-COASTF says which failed.
    ' BOUND: DAT coastLoMs .. coastHiMs at the row (12 V 62 .. 738 ms, 24 V 71 .. 834): the analysis's bracket (sec 1.2) at
    '  its two corners, (J / Bv) ln(1 + Bv w / Tc) from the 100 % speed (P-C, sec 8 L1), rounded outward, the lower less
    '  the reader's resolution (CON { the Doco's numbers }, THE COAST). MODELED.
    ' CORRECT CASE: the central bracket (J 4e-6, Tc 0.003, Bv 1e-5) reads 228 ms at 12 V, 256 at 24 V; the corners 66 /
    '  732 and 73 / 827 (sgl2b_model.py, the reader mirrored at 2 kHz) -> PASS. Broken: a motor whose J or friction lies
    '  outside the bracket ("a coast of seconds", the analysis's falsifier) reads 3_000 -> FAIL, and the model is refitted;
    '  the leg leaving holdAtStop(TRUE) makes FR_SHIPPED SHORT the phases, which brake 2,238 rpm to rest in 24 ms (28 at
    '  24 V) -> FAIL. Desk mutation: the rest instant taken at the END of the quiet run adds REST_QUIET_MS and FAILs the
    '  bracket's longest corner (1_033 ms). UNFIXED: none, a first measurement of the motor.
    '  Rival: a coast lengthened because something still drove the bridge (a re-synced stop on the ramp: 3.7 s from 12 V's
    '  top) rather than by J and friction: state_ok (DCS_FAULTED at every reading) separates them, and makes it NOMEAS; a
    '  coast shortened by a shorted bridge rather than by friction: hold (isHoldAtStop() at the fault) separates them.

    ' R23-SGL-LEADMOVE (L-offscan, the lead check), crit LEAD_SPREAD_X10, units DEG_X10, one instance per increment sign:
    '  the spread (largest less smallest) of the RESOLVED vertices across the three speeds, of the fit LEADMOVE_FITQ names.
    '  PHASE 2c (arbiter decision D9): the DUTY fit is primary, for this cell and for the Z reference (B1-OFSPAIR mid_x10 /
    '  lead_x10); the DC-link fit is SECONDARY, recorded beside it in B1-OFSPAIR (dc_*) and B1-OFSFIT q DC, because Rev A
    '  was taken not to resolve the unloaded 20-110 mA DC-link minimum (phase 2b's sgl2b_model.py) and a cell NOMEAS by
    '  construction is an incomplete test (doctrine overlay P10).
    ' PRECONDITION: at least two speeds' fits of LEADMOVE_FITQ RESOLVED (each vertex's standard error <=
    '  OFS_VERT_SE_MAX_X10, the vertex inside +-OFS_SPAN_DEG); otherwise NOMEAS, and B1-OFSFIT says why.
    ' BOUND: 0 .. LEADMOVE_TOL_X10 (100: 10 degrees): the analysis's P-S5 negative, "the best offset moving > 10 degrees
    '  between 25 % and 100 %". PROVISIONAL (arbiter): two vertices on a 5 degree grid, each good to 2.5 degrees.
    ' CORRECT CASE (the duty fit, sgl2c_model.py part 1b, the analysis's own steady-state plant doco_need() through this
    '  harness's ofsFit()): the duty vertex resolves at 25 and 50 % in 200 of 200 noisy trials (+-5 counts) -- 12 V at
    '  0.5 mH reads 6.5 / 12.9 degrees, its 100 % vertex outside the span (unresolved) -> 64 -> PASS. Broken: a current
    '  minimum moving 15 degrees between 25 and 100 % reads 129 on either fit -> FAIL, a finding (plan sec 6's conditional
    '  lead schedule). UNFIXED: none, a first measurement; the 6.5in's lead fell from ~20 degrees at a crawl to 5-8.
    '  THE DUTY FIT'S OWN RIVAL, from the same plant (sgl2c_model.py part 1): at a fixed lead the 6.1.0 trim leaves only
    '  the duty free, and the duty is LEAST where the voltage leads the back-EMF by atan(X/R) = atan(w L / R), not where
    '  the current is least (the d-axis current is then E sin(atan(X/R)) / Z). So the duty vertex sits 7-61 degrees AHEAD of
    '  the current minimum and MOVES WITH SPEED by 20-37 degrees between 25 and 100 % (Lh 0.5-1.5 mH) while the current
    '  minimum moves 0.3-1.3. At 24 V, 0.5 mH, all three duty vertices resolve (7.7 / 14.5 / 19.8) and the cell FAILS a
    '  motor whose current minimum does not move, 200 of 200 trials; elsewhere it passes only because the 100 % vertex
    '  leaves the span. THE SEPARATING READING is the DC-link fit beside it: in the same plant the DC link at 30 degrees
    '  off the minimum is 4-50 x its value there (19 -> 83-115 mA at 25 %, 108 -> 504-5,047 mA at 100 %, 12 V; part 1a),
    '  not the 1.15 x phase 2b's I0 / cos(d) assumed, and it resolves at every speed in 187-200 of 200 trials, its spread
    '  1-7 degrees (part 1b). A duty spread with a DC spread under the bound is atan(X/R), not a lead. The arbiter's ruling
    '  on D9 against this is asked in the phase 2c hand-back; LEADMOVE_FITQ is the one constant it turns.
    '  Rivals for either fit: hall edges that lag more with speed move a vertex with no change of lead -- B1-OFSZ's z_x10 at
    '  the same speeds separates them; the sense zero drifting between sides moves the DC-link curve -- B1-OFSFIT's
    '  ref_drift_ma.
    LEADMOVE_TOL_X10 = 100
    LEADMOVE_FITQ    = FITQ_DC                              ' arbiter decision D10 (reverses D9): the duty vertex sits atan(wL/R) ahead of the current minimum and moves with speed; the DC-link fit resolves (2c model, 187-200 of 200)

    ' R23-SGL-PASSPRD (L-passprb), crit PASS_DEV_PPM, units PPM, one instance per increment sign: the encoder's speed over
    '  the window against |incr| x 360 counts per electrical cycle x clkfreq / (frame_cnt x DRIVE_PASS_FRAMES) / 2^32, ppm.
    ' PRECONDITION: the drive arrived at the command; the window ran PASSPRB_WIN_MS with no fault, no re-sync and no held
    '  pass (a held pass stops the field, so it is no longer incr x rate); the encoder agreed with the halls over it
    '  (bWindowEncOk()). Otherwise NOMEAS.
    ' BOUND: -PASSPRD_TOL_PPM .. +PASSPRD_TOL_PPM (1_000): plan sec 1.4, "to +-0.1 %". Its floor: a 22-frame pass rarer
    '  than 1 in 43 reads inside it (1 in 50: +869; 1 in 40: +1_085).
    ' CORRECT CASE: DRIVER_REV 50's pass is 23 frames at every clock -> -3 .. 0 ppm at the six clock names (a count is 4
    '  ppm at 268,560) -> PASS. UNFIXED (DRIVER_REV 49, PL-50's 2-22 clock margin): every pass at 22 frames reads +45_452;
    '  one pass in 20 +2_176 -> FAIL. Desk mutations: the window timed by one signed getct() difference wraps past 2^31
    '  clocks (10 s at 270 MHz is 2.7e9) -> -2.7e6 -> FAIL; the rate from the nominal 44 kHz reads the frame's rounding,
    '  -268 ppm at clk-floor, and microseconds from clkfreq / 1_000_000 read -824 at clk-frac -- inside the bound, each
    '  hiding most of a real error, which is why neither is used (sgl2b_model.py).
    '  Rival: a short PWM frame reads fast exactly as a short pass does; test_bench_t0's frame-budget cell (the 6.5in
    '  session, plan sec 1.4) measures the frame. A slipping coupling or a slipped pole pair reads SLOW: wchk and held
    '  separate them.
    PASSPRD_TOL_PPM = 1_000

    ' ---- PHASE 2c cells. Every negative named below is a desk mutation of this harness's own arithmetic or a stated
    '  physical case, run in the python model sgl2c_model.py part 2 (task 3679 phase 2c; 43 of 43 checks agree); every
    '  correct-case number is DERIVED, the analysis's, or that model's.

    ' R23-SGL-LIMHOLD (L-handload), crit FAULT_RUNS, units COUNT, instances LIM-4A and LIM-2A (the test limits; the
    '  default step folds nothing by prediction, P-H1, so it is no test of the limit): the faults and re-synced faults
    '  from his grip to the step's end, of the step's last run.
    ' PRECONDITION: the encoder saw his grip (its speed under HAND_CONTACT_PM of the command) AND the fold-back engaged at
    '  least once since the drive began (getEventTotal(EV_FOLDBACK)): a load the limit met. The drive cannot erase what
    '  the encoder read; a grip too light to fold is not a test of the limit. Otherwise NOMEAS (REDO, a firmer grip).
    '  TASK 3686 (the exclusion check): a fault after his grip is judged WITH OR WITHOUT a fold -- a limit that never
    '  acts and then lets the rotor fault is this cell's own negative, and the fold precondition read it NOMEAS
    '  (sgl3686_model.py: now 1 -> FAIL). A clean grip with no fold stays NOMEAS (the light touch below).
    ' BOUND: 0 .. 0: plan sec 7, "the limit holds (no lag fault)".
    ' CORRECT CASE: P-H3 (MODELED, analysis 4.1): at 4 A and 2 A the limit hold arms (set-backs 6-399) and no run faults
    '  -> 0 -> PASS. Broken: a lag fault under the hand -> 1 -> FAIL. Desk mutation: without the fold precondition a light
    '  touch reads 0 and PASSES a limit that never acted. UNFIXED: none on the Doco; the 6.5in's floor-grab held at 2 A.
    '  Rival: a fault from the supply sagging under the stall (a bench supply's own limit), not the drive: B1-HANDD's
    '  dc_peak_ma against the supply's limit and the fault's cause separate them.
    LIMHOLD_LO = 0
    LIMHOLD_HI = 0

    ' R23-SGL-BLKSTOP (L-handload), crit LATCH_MS, units MS, instances LIM-4A, LIM-2A and (12 V only) LIM-DEF: the blocked
    '  stop's latch, timed from the shaft's last hall tick, of the step's last run; a stand of HAND_NOLATCH_MS with no
    '  latch reads HAND_NOLATCH_MS (a FAIL, never a NOMEAS).
    ' PRECONDITION: AT_SPEED reached, his grip seen, and then either the latch (getProtectiveStop() ERR_PLATFORM_BLOCKED)
    '  or the shaft standing still -- no hall tick -- for HAND_NOLATCH_MS. A grip that kept the shaft creeping never
    '  stands, and is NOMEAS (the panel says so; REDO). The stand is read on the driver's hall position, which the stop
    '  cannot erase: it is what the stop is meant to see. TASK 3686 (the exclusion check): this cell's negatives -- no
    '  latch (read HAND_NOLATCH_MS) and a latch out of the band -- are both measured; a creeping grip is the stop's own
    '  reason not to latch (the stimulus not applied), and a fault before the stand is LIMHOLD's measured FAIL.
    ' BOUND: BLKSTOP_LO_MS (988) .. BLKSTOP_HI_MS (1_168), the plan's BLKSTOP band carried from the 6.5in (test_bench_dual's
    '  BLK_STAND_LO_MS and, before its SRC_REV 76, its upper bound): the library's BLOCKED_PASSES slots of 1 ms (1_000),
    '  less / plus HAND_STAMP_MS 12 for the stamps (the tick is stamped by the first 5 ms reading that shows it, the latch
    '  by its EV_STOP event's own getms()), plus 156 ms the 6.5in's field took to reach LAG_SOFT. DERIVED for the Doco: at
    '  power 10 the field reaches LAG_SOFT 9 ms after a stall, and under a test limit the limiter half (PL-179 F-a) starts
    '  the count at once, so the upper end is generous here.
    ' CORRECT CASE: the count beginning 0-10 ms after the last tick reads 995 .. 1_009 (2,000 trials) -> PASS; P-H2's
    '  model latches 6 of 6 at 1,003-1,169 ms after CONTACT (one past the band) -- timed from the tick it reads ~1,005.
    '  Broken: no blocked stop -> 1_180 -> FAIL; BLOCKED_PASSES 500 -> 501 -> FAIL. Desk mutation: timed from his grip
    '  instead of the last tick, a 300 ms creep reads 1_455 and FAILs a correct driver -- why the tick is the origin;
    '  HAND_NOLATCH_MS inside the band would stop a correct driver before its latch -- why it sits past the band's top.
    '  UNFIXED: the 6.5in's floor obstacle latched in band (PL-106); P-H1: at the default limits 4 of 6 contact points
    '  latch, a creeping grip never does.
    '  Rival: a latch that came from the shaft stopping BEFORE his hand (a supply that browned out at the stall): the
    '  encoder's grip time against the last tick (B1-HAND contact_ms, last_tick_ms) separates them.
    HAND_STAMP_MS   = 2 * SAMPLE_MS + 2
    BLK_PASS_MS     = wheel.BLOCKED_PASSES * wheel.MS_PER_SEC / wheel.FRONT_LOOP_HZ    ' 1_000
    BLK_FIELD_MS    = 156                                   ' the 6.5in's allowance for the field to reach LAG_SOFT (carried)
    BLKSTOP_LO_MS   = BLK_PASS_MS - HAND_STAMP_MS           ' 988
    BLKSTOP_HI_MS   = BLK_PASS_MS + BLK_FIELD_MS + HAND_STAMP_MS                      ' 1_168
    HAND_NOLATCH_MS = BLKSTOP_HI_MS + HAND_STAMP_MS         ' 1_180: a stand this long with no latch, and the program stops it

    ' R23-SGL-HOLDRISE (L-heldpush), crit RISE_MS, units MS, instances RISE and FALL (the halls' measured direction of the
    '  push): the hold's rise to its ceiling by its RATE -- the duty gained over the reading pairs displaced, under the
    '  ceiling and HS_HOLDING at both ends, scaled to (ceiling - duty_min) (T0-24's rule, PL-130: the rise counts only
    '  displaced time, so how firmly or how steadily he turns cannot enter it); -1 when the duty rose before any
    '  displacement (P-H4: "duty stays at duty_min until 15 degrees").
    ' PRECONDITION: a fresh hold (HS_HOLDING at displacement 0, armed this step, the stop mode re-selected: T0-24's re-arm,
    '  PL-123) and at least RISE_MIN_SPAN_MS of rising pairs; otherwise NOMEAS (a flick through the sector: the panel
    '  says turn slower). The hold cannot erase his displacement: the halls read it.
    '  TASK 3686 (the exclusion check): a hold displaced RISE_MIN_SPAN_MS or more whose duty gained NOTHING reads
    '  HOLDRISE_NONE_MS -- a hold that does not push back is this cell's own negative, and the rate's "gain above 0"
    '  read it NOMEAS (sgl3686_model.py: now 99_999 -> FAIL).
    ' BOUND: HOLDRISE_LO_MS (220) .. HOLDRISE_HI_MS (280): the library's HOLD_RISE_MS 250 less / plus a reading either end,
    '  T0-24's band (T0_24_HOLD_RISE_LO_MS / _HI_MS).
    ' CORRECT CASE: frontHold() under a hand at 20 or 60 deg/s, pausing or not, resting anywhere in its sector -> 249 ->
    '  PASS. Broken: HOLD_RISE_MS 500 -> 500; DRIVER_REV 17's truncated step -> 550; a hold that rises on time from its
    '  arming, not on displacement -> -1: each FAIL. UNFIXED: T0-24 measured 250 on the 6.5in (Visit 10, PL-130 closed).
    '  Rival: a rise that is slow because the halls missed the displacement (a hand turning back and forth across the
    '  first edge) rather than the hold: B1-HPUSH's edges and first_edge_cnt separate them.
    HOLDRISE_LO_MS    = wheel.HOLD_RISE_MS - 30
    HOLDRISE_HI_MS    = wheel.HOLD_RISE_MS + 30
    RISE_MIN_SPAN_MS  = 50
    RISE_NOT_SEEN     = -2                                  ' B1-HPUSH rise_ms NA: too little rising time to rate (-1 is P-H4's negative)
    HOLDRISE_NONE_MS  = 99_999                              ' task 3686: displaced RISE_MIN_SPAN_MS with no rise at all (a FAIL)

    ' R23-SGL-HOLDSLIP (L-heldpush), crit SLIP_TICKS, units TICKS, instances RISE and FALL: the net hall ticks of the push
    '  -- the encoder object's captured edges, classified by this harness's own order table -- at the first reading of
    '  HS_SLIPPED, of the direction's last run.
    ' PRECONDITION: a fresh hold, as HOLDRISE's, and HS_SLIPPED read, no captured edge lost; otherwise NOMEAS (a hold
    '  that let go at its time limit instead is HS_LIMITED, and says so). TASK 3686 (the exclusion check): a hold that
    '  let go at its time limit AFTER the push had passed more than HOLD_SLIP_TICKS net ticks never slipped where its
    '  defaults say -- this cell's own negative, which HS_SLIPPED's precondition read NOMEAS -- and reads the net ticks
    '  at the limit (sgl3686_model.py: 4 -> FAIL). A push that stopped short of the slip and met the limit stays NOMEAS.
    ' BOUND: wheel.HOLD_SLIP_TICKS .. wheel.HOLD_SLIP_TICKS (2): the library's own slip (P-H4, "the slip comes at 30
    '  degrees" -- two 15 degree ticks, 15-30 degrees from where it rested, B1-HPUSH's slip_cnt).
    ' CORRECT CASE: frontHold() under a hand, any rest in the sector, a slow hand or a 600 deg/s flick -> 2 -> PASS.
    '  Broken: HOLD_SLIP_TICKS 1 -> 1 -> FAIL; 3 -> 3 -> FAIL. UNFIXED: T0-24's HOLD-SLIP passed on the 6.5in.
    '  Rival: a hand fast enough to cross a third edge within one 5 ms reading reads 3 with the hold correct: B1-HPUSH's
    '  turn rate at the slip (slip_dps) separates them (it needs over 3,000 degrees a second).

    ' R23-SGL-SAGTYPE (L-sag, OPTIONAL), crit FAULT_FIRST, units BOOL01, one instance TOP: 1 when a fault (or a re-sync)
    '  came before the encoder's speed fell under SAG_LOST_PM of its command for SAG_LOST_MS, 0 when the slip came first.
    ' PRECONDITION: the row's top reached (AT_SPEED) and held through SAG_SETTLE_MS, then one of the two seen within
    '  SAG_WAIT_MS of the operator's dial-down; otherwise NOMEAS (not dialled far enough: REDO). The fault flag and the
    '  re-sync count are the driver's own record of the fault, read before the encoder at every reading.
    ' BOUND: DAT sagExpectFault at the row, both ends: 1 at 22.2 V (470e6: the field's 28.0 counts a pass pass the
    '  25-count margin, PK-1), 0 at 18.5 V (398e6, 23.7 counts, under it). The analysis's P-S7 outcome TYPE (sec 5.3).
    ' CORRECT CASE: P-S7 (MODELED, docosag): 470e6 faults at 17.67 V -> 1 -> PASS; 398e6 slips at 7.75 V -> 0 -> PASS.
    '  Broken: 470e6 slipping without a fault -> 0 -> FAIL (the analysis's falsifier); 398e6 faulting -> 1 -> FAIL.
    '  Desk mutation: the encoder alone, without the fault flag, reads a fault-first motor's re-synced stop as a slip
    '  (0) and FAILs it -- why the flag is read first. UNFIXED: none; a first measurement, and PK-1's evidence.
    '  Rival: a supply that collapses (its own current limit) rather than a smooth dial: B1-SAGPT's duty trace (a step, not
    '  a ramp) separates them.

    ' ---- TASK 3686: the D2 qualification's new cells (plan sec 7). Every negative named below is a desk mutation of
    '  this harness's own arithmetic or a stated physical case, run in the python model sgl3686_model.py (51 of 51
    '  checks agree); every correct-case number is that model's or DERIVED. Their sign-off task is 3686.

    ' R23-SGL-START (L-wiring), crit START_WIRE_OK, units BOOL01, one instance MOTOR: 1 when the public start path and the
    '  wiring walk both pass -- start() (setStartChecks(TRUE): a failed check refuses it) returned a cog that reported
    '  ready in READY_TIMEOUT_MS, and after checkWiring() returned NO_ERROR, getHealth() reads HLT_WIRING among the
    '  checks run and none of HLT_ALL_CHECKS or HLT_WIRING failed -- else 0. A criterion of more than one condition (the
    '  plan's "the start checks and checkWiring() pass"), so a boolean cell; B1-START (the checks) and B1-WIRING (the
    '  walk) carry each condition's readings.
    ' PRECONDITION: start() was attempted (the board read Rev A before it: the bench's own safety, plan sec 2) and then
    '  either refused, or started and never reported ready -- each a measured 0 -- or started and the walk ran.
    '  Otherwise NOMEAS: the started board read other than Rev A, the test limit was not taken, or the encoder did not
    '  start. THE EXCLUSION CHECK: the negatives are a failed HLT_* check (start() refuses: 0) and a
    '  failed HLT_WIRING (0); none of the exclusions is either. A board start() would refuse for its board never
    '  reaches start(): that is the bench statement's check (plan sec 2), not this cell's negative. The walk runs
    '  before the harness reads the rest zero (bMeasureZero()), so that check cannot exclude it; HLT_SENSE_ZERO, the
    '  same band, refuses the start first and reads 0.
    ' BOUND: START_OK .. START_OK (1): plan sec 7, "the start checks and checkWiring() pass".
    ' CORRECT CASE: a sound motor, every check and the walk pass -> 1 -> PASS. Broken: a hall line open (HLT_HALLS) or a
    '  phase lead open (HLT_PHASE_V) refuses the start -> 0; two phases swapped (HLT_WIRING) -> 0; the walk's request
    '  unanswered (ERR_NO_RESPONSE) -> 0: each FAIL. Desk mutations: judged on checkWiring()'s return alone, a swapped
    '  pair reads 1 and PASSES (it returns NO_ERROR whatever its verdict) -- why getHealth() is read; without the
    '  checked bit a walk that judged nothing reads 1 -- why HLT_WIRING must be among the checks run. UNFIXED: D1's
    '  B1-START records today's checks on every run; checkWiring() ran at D1 only in the doco-demo tiers.
    '  Rival: a walk that fails because its pass band was derived on the 6.5in (WALK_SHORT_TICKS, WALK_OVERSHOOT_TICKS)
    '  and the Doco's light rotor overshoots it, not because the wiring is wrong: B1-WIRING's fwd_ticks / rev_ticks
    '  against the encoder's own excursion (enc_hi, enc_lo: one count an electrical degree) separate them -- a correct
    '  motor overshoots both legs alike with the encoder agreeing with the halls; a miswired one moves the wrong way,
    '  or not at all.
    START_OK      = 1

    ' R23-SGL-POWER (L-power), crit PWR_DEV_PM, units PERMILLE, one instance per POWER sign (PWR-POS, PWR-NEG: the API's
    '  own sign; B1-POWER prints the increment's beside it): the worst |encoder speed / the drive law of the increment
    '  the library wrote for the power - 1| over the sign's rungs, DAT powerPcts capped at the row's top power; a rung
    '  that faulted, or that the library refused, reads PM (it did not hold its speed).
    ' PRECONDITION: the rung was commanded by driveAtPower() and its window ran (arrived, or measured as far as it got in
    '  its bound; then LADDER_SETTLE_MS and the LADDER_WINDOW_MS window), or it faulted, or it was refused; a rung a
    '  guard ended is not judged (the run is over). The speed is the encoder's travel over the window's own getct()
    '  span. THE EXCLUSION CHECK: a window is dropped only when the encoder disagrees with the driver's hall position
    '  (bWindowEncOk(), and the run ends) -- both read the rotor, so a rotor behind its field (the negative) agrees with
    '  the halls and is never the excluded case.
    ' BOUND: 0 .. POWER_TOL_PM (30): plan sec 7, "each power rung holds speed: encoder speed within 3 % of command" (the
    '  6.5in's SPINRATE_FOL_LO 97): FOLLOW's bar, on the power path.
    ' CORRECT CASE: every row, both signs, a synchronous rotor -> 0 .. 1 -> PASS. Broken: the rotor at 96.0 % of its
    '  field -> 41 -> FAIL; a rung that faulted or was refused -> 1_000 -> FAIL. Desk mutations: a refused top counted
    '  NOMEAS leaves its sign judged on three rungs -> PASS -- why a refusal reads PM; the reference taken as the power's
    '  nominal share of the ceiling, not the increment written, reads up to 31 for a synchronous rotor (the map's
    '  minimum and its truncated slope) and FAILS a correct motor -- why the written increment is the reference.
    '  UNFIXED: D1's R23-SGL-FOLLOW over the same speeds by increment (the arbiter's D7) and its L-ramp tops by power;
    '  the 11.1 V row's top is predicted to fault (P-S2) until sec 6 changes its ceiling.
    '  Rival: the test current limit holding the rotor back (fold-back, held passes), not the drive's speed control:
    '  B1-POWER's folds, held and capped separate them -- a slow rung with folds is the limit, with none the field.
    POWER_TOL_PM  = FOLLOW_TOL_PM

    ' R23-SGL-TOPSPD (L-ladder, L-ramp), crit TOP_DEV_PM, units PERMILLE, instances NEG and POS -- the ceiling: the
    '  ladder's 100 % rung from rest and by a step, and L-ramp's top run -- and REVERSAL (L-ramp's three tops): the worst
    '  |encoder speed / the speed law at the increment - 1| over the ceiling's windows, two-sided; a run that faulted,
    '  or whose window never ran (the climb did not arrive in its bound), reads PM. Its instances and feeds are
    '  R23-SGL-SMOOTH's, which judges the same runs' faults and re-syncs.
    ' PRECONDITION: the run was commanded and driven to its window's end, to its fault or to its bound; a run a guard
    '  ended, or whose window the encoder check refused (bWindowEncOk(), and the run ends), is not judged. THE EXCLUSION
    '  CHECK: as POWER's -- the encoder check compares two readings of the rotor, so a rotor off the speed law is not
    '  what it excludes; a climb that never arrives reads PM rather than being dropped.
    ' BOUND: 0 .. TOPSPD_TOL_PM (20): TOPSPD's bar, the 6.5in's LIMTOP_FOLLOW_PCT 98 (test_bench_dual.spin2's
    '  R18-DUAL-TOPSPD-M: a ceiling rung clean at >= 98 % of the speed law), made TWO-SIDED: the encoder needs no tick
    '  quantisation allowance (the 6.5in widened its band by rateBandPct()), and a field fast of the law is a defect too.
    ' CORRECT CASE: every row's top, a 5 s or a 2 s window, a synchronous rotor -> 0 .. 1 -> PASS. Broken: the rotor at
    '  97.5 % -> 25 -> FAIL, where FOLLOW's 3 % PASSES it; every pass 22 frames (DRIVER_REV 49's 2-22 clock margin) ->
    '  +45 -> FAIL; one held pass in 40 -> 26 -> FAIL; a climb that never arrived -> 1_000 -> FAIL. Desk mutation: the
    '  6.5in's one-sided ">= 98 %" PASSES the 22-frame field -- why the bound is two-sided. UNFIXED: D1's L-ramp hold
    '  following (B1-RAMP hold_fol_pm) and ladder ceiling (B1-RUNG fol_pm) are today's reading of it.
    '  Rival: a supply that cannot hold the top (the duty pinned) rather than a drive off its law: the window's capped
    '  and held counts (B1-RUNGD capped, held; B1-RAMP held) separate them -- off the law with no capped pass is the
    '  drive's own timing; with capped passes, the supply or the ceiling's duty reserve.
    TOPSPD_TOL_PM = 20

CON { record widths -- every numeric field is clamped to one of these }

    LIM_TINY  = benchLog.LIM_TINY                           ' prints at most 4 bytes: -999
    LIM_SMALL = benchLog.LIM_SMALL                          ' prints at most 7 bytes: -99_999
    LIM_MID   = benchLog.LIM_MID                            ' prints at most 10 bytes: -9_999_999
    LIM_BIG   = benchLog.LIM_BIG                            ' prints at most 12 bytes: -999_999_999

    ' token field length limits (a longer token prints as "?")
    TOKMAX_CFG       = 8
    TOKMAX_BOARD     = 7
    TOKMAX_INST      = 8                                    ' a SIGNOFF instance: a set, a sign, a sign-change or sign-kind, REVERSAL
    TOKMAX_ENTRY     = 4
    TOKMAX_RO        = 8
    TOKMAX_SR        = 14
    TOKMAX_SET       = 8
    TOKMAX_SIGN      = 3
    TOKMAX_DIR       = 4
    TOKMAX_OUTCOME   = 12
    TOKMAX_REASON    = 9
    TOKMAX_BIN       = 6
    TOKMAX_CELL      = 20
    TOKMAX_CRIT      = 18
    TOKMAX_TASK      = 5
    TOKMAX_UNITS     = 8
    TOKMAX_SFVERDICT = 9
    TOKMAX_LEG       = 8
    TOKMAX_SIDE      = 5
    TOKMAX_FITQ      = 4
    TOKMAX_HE        = 8                                    ' phase 2c: a hand-load step's end
    TOKMAX_SO        = 11                                   ' a sag's outcome
    TOKMAX_PH        = 8                                    ' a panel phase or whole-run screen
    TOKMAX_BT        = 10                                   ' a button, MISS or IGNORED

CON { the hand tests' panel -- GENERATED by tools/gen_single_assets.py, do not hand-edit }

' Layers: 1 background, 2 step names / whole-run names / told supplies, 3 banners, 4 cards, 5 digits,
' 6 status phrases, 7 reading labels, 8 buttons. A DEBUG backtick command takes the layer as a literal, so
' the layer numbers live in sgSetupPanel() / sgDraw() and here only as this comment.

    SG_STEP_COUNT            = 8
    SG_PHASE_COUNT           = 6
    SG_SNUM_X                = 64
    SG_SCOUNT_X              = 126
    SG_STEP_LINE_Y           = 34
    SG_NAME_X                = 160
    SG_NAME_W                = 266
    SG_NAME_H                = 36
    SG_SUP_X                 = 432
    SG_SUP_W                 = 116
    SG_NAME_SPECIAL0         = 8
    SG_SUPPLY_ROW0           = 11
    SG_BAN_X                 = 12
    SG_BAN_Y                 = 76
